owed by the rest.\n\nWait, let me think again. Let's consider the positions:\n\nThe numbers are:\n\nFirst number: 8 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 2 (units)\n\nSecond number: 2 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 1 (units)\n\nAdding them:\n\nHundred millions: 8 + 2 = 10. So write 0, carry 1.\n\nTen millions: 2 + 0 = 2. Plus carryover 1 = 3. So 3, no carryover.\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7. No carryover.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 + 5 = 6. No carryover.\n\nTen thousands: 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 0 + 4 = 4. No carryover.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 1 = 7. No carryover.\n\nTens: 2 + 9 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nUnits: 2 + 1 = 3. No carryover.\n\nWait, hold on, this is conflicting with the previous breakdown. Wait, maybe I messed up the positions.\n\nWait, perhaps I need to align the numbers properly by place value. Let me write them out with place values:\n\nFirst number: 824,190,622\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- 8 * 100,000,000\n\n- 2 * 10,000,000\n\n- 4 * 1,000,000\n\n- 1 * 100,000\n\n- 9 * 10,000\n\n- 0 * 1,000\n\n- 6 * 100\n\n- 2 * 10\n\n- 2 * 1\n\nSecond number: 203,514,191\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- 2 * 100,000,000\n\n- 0 * 10,000,000\n\n- 3 * 1,000,000\n\n- 5 * 100,000\n\n- 1 * 10,000\n\n- 4 * 1,000\n\n- 1 * 100\n\n- 9 * 10\n\n- 1 * 1\n\nNow, adding them by place value:\n\n100,000,000: 8 + 2 = 10. So 0 with carryover 1.\n\n10,000,000: 2 + 0 = 2. No carryover.\n\n1,000,000: 4 + 3 = 7. No carryover.\n\n100,000: 1 + 5 = 6. No carryover.\n\n10,000: 9 + 1 = 10. So 0 with carryover 1.\n\n1,000: 0 + 4 = 4. No carryover.\n\n100: 6 + 1 = 7. No carryover.\n\n10: 2 + 9 = 11. So 1 with carryover 1.\n\n1: 2 + 1 = 3. No carryover.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nCarryover 1 at the beginning, then 0 (from 100,000,000), then 2, 7, 6, 0 (from 10,000), 4, 7, 1 (from 10), 3.\n\nWait, but that would be 1