units) + 6 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n7 (tens) + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n8 (hundreds) + 9 = 17 + 1 = 18 \u2192 8, carry 1\n\n3 (thousands) + 9 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n9 (ten thousands) + 4 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n8 (hundred thousands) + 3 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n0 (millions) + 9 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n0 (ten millions) + 0 = 0 + 0 = 0, carry 1\n\n8 (hundred millions) + 0 = 8 + 0 = 8, carry 0\n\n3 (billions) + 0 = 3 + 0 = 3\n\nSo the sum is 83,072,349,913.\n\nWait, but let me check with another approach. Let's convert both numbers to numbers and add them.\n\nFirst number: 83,008,893,877\n\nSecond number: 60,003,499,926\n\nAdding them:\n\n83,008,893,877\n\n+60,003,499,926\n\n= (83,008,893,877 + 60,003,499,926)\n\nLet's add the millions:\n\n83,008,893,877 is 83,008,893,877\n\n60,003,499,926 is 60,003,499,926\n\nAdding the two:\n\n83,008,893,877 + 60,003,499,926\n\n= (83,008,893,877 + 60,000,000,000) + 3,499,926\n\n= 143,008,893,877 + 3,499,926\n\n= 143,008,893,877 + 3,499,926\n\n= 143,012,393,803\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 83,008,893,877 + 60,003,499,926.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 83,008,893,877 + 60,003,499,926.\n\nBreak it down:\n\n83,008,893,877 + 60,000,000,000 = 143,008,893,877\n\nThen add the remaining 3,499,926:\n\n143,008,893,877 + 3,499,926 = ?\n\n143,008,893,877 + 3,000,000 = 143,011,893,877\n\n143,011,893,877 + 499,926 = 143,012,393,803\n\nSo total is 143,012,393,803.\n\nBut earlier, when adding digit by digit, I got 83,072,349,913. That can't be right. There's a mistake here. Wait, 83,072,349,913 is way smaller than 143,012,393,803. So clearly, the digit-by-digit addition was wrong.\n\nWait, where did I go wrong? Let's check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number: 83,008,893,877\n\nSecond number: 60,003,499,926\n\nAdding these two.\n\nLet me write them out without commas:\n\nFirst number: 83008893877\n\nSe