n\nBillions place: 8 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 8 + 0 = 8, carry 0\n\nTen billions place: 0 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 0 + 0 = 0, carry 0\n\nHundred billions place: 8 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nWait, but the second number's hundred billions place is 0, so we shouldn't have a carryover here. So the hundred billions place is 8 + 6 = 14, so 4 with a carryover of 1. But since there's no higher place value to carry over to, we just write 4.\n\nSo putting all the digits together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 3\n\nTens: 1\n\nHundreds: 0\n\nThousands: 3\n\nTen thousands: 4\n\nHundred thousands: 2\n\nMillions: 8\n\nTen millions: 1\n\nHundred millions: 3\n\nBillions: 8\n\nTen billions: 0\n\nHundred billions: 4\n\nSo the sum is 408,317,531,313.\n\nWait, but this contradicts the previous result of 143,012,393,803. There must be a mistake in the digit positions.\n\nWait, let's check the alignment again. The first number is 83,008,893,877 and the second is 60,003,499,926. Let's write them out with the same number of digits by adding leading zeros to the shorter one:\n\nFirst number: 83,008,893,877\n\nSecond number: 060,003,499,926\n\nNow, adding:\n\n          83,008,893,877\n\n        +  060,003,499,926\n\n        ---------------------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 6 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n8 + 2 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 9 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n9 + 9 = 18 + 1 = 19 \u2192 9, carry 1\n\n8 + 4 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n0 + 3 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\n0 + 9 = 9\n\n8 + 0 = 8\n\n0 + 0 = 0\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\nWait, this is not matching. Wait, maybe I need to write the numbers with commas in the correct places.\n\nFirst number: 83,008,893,877\n\nSecond number: 60,003,499,926\n\nSo when adding:\n\n83,008,893,877\n\n+60,003,499,926\n\nThe digits are:\n\nFirst number: 8 3 0 0 8 8 9 3 8 7 7\n\nSecond number: 6 0 0 0 3 4 9 9 9 2 6\n\nNow, adding digit by digit:\n\nPos