177\n\n113,827,3177 + 50 = 113,827,3227\n\n113,827,3227 + 90 = 113,827,3317\n\n113,827,3317 + 8 = 113,827,3325\n\nYes, that's correct. So the sum is 113,827,3325. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 238,556,36. Which is impossible. Therefore, there must be a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition.\n\nWait, but how? Let me check the digit-by-digit addition again. Maybe I added the digits in the wrong order.\n\nWait, the first number is 63,726,9777. So the digits from right to left are:\n\nPosition 1: 7 (ones)\n\nPosition 2: 7 (tens)\n\nPosition 3: 9 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 4: 6 (thousands)\n\nPosition 5: 2 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 6: 6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 7: 7 (millions)\n\nPosition 8: 3 (ten millions)\n\nSimilarly, the second number is 50,128,6598:\n\nPosition 1: 9 (ones)\n\nPosition 2: 5 (tens)\n\nPosition 3: 6 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 4: 8 (thousands)\n\nPosition 5: 2 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 6: 1 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 7: 0 (millions)\n\nPosition 8: 5 (ten millions)\n\nWait, no. Wait, when adding, the digits should be aligned by their place value. So the first number is:\n\nTen millions: 6\n\nMillions: 3\n\nHundred thousands: 7\n\nTen thousands: 2\n\nThousands: 6\n\nHundreds: 9\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 7\n\nThe second number is:\n\nTen millions: 5\n\nMillions: 0\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 2\n\nThousands: 8\n\nHundreds: 6\n\nTens: 5\n\nOnes: 9\n\nSo when adding, we should add the digits in the same position:\n\nOnes: 7 + 9 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nTens: 7 + 5 = 12 + 1 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 6 + 8 = 14 + 1 = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 2 + 2 = 4 + 1 = 5. Write 5, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 1 = 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nMillions: 3 + 0 = 3. Write 3, no carry.\n\nTen millions: 1 + 1 = 2. Write 2.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nTen millions: 2\n\nMillions: 3\n\nHundred thousands: 8\n\nTen thousands: 5\n\nThousands: 5\n\nHundreds: 6\n\nTen