+ 7 = 14. Add the carried 1? Wait, no. Wait, the first number has 7 in the ten thousands place, the second has 7 as well. So 7 + 7 = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n\nNext (hundred thousands place): 7 + 8 = 15. Add the carried 1? Wait, no. Wait, the first number has 7 here, the second has 8. So 7 + 8 = 15. Write down 5, carry over 1.\n\nNext (millions place): 5 + 3 = 8. Add the carried 1? Wait, no. Wait, the first number has 5 in the millions place, the second has 3. So 5 + 3 = 8. No carryover. Write down 8.\n\nNext (ten millions place): 7 (from first number) + 5 (from second number) = 12. Write down 2, carry over 1.\n\nFinally, the hundred millions place: 5 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) = 8, plus the carried 1 makes 9.\n\nSo putting all those together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 8\n\nTens: 2\n\nHundreds: 4\n\nThousands: 4\n\nTen thousands: 4\n\nHundred thousands: 5\n\nMillions: 8\n\nTen millions: 2\n\nHundred millions: 9\n\nSo the sum is 92,544,6428? Wait, wait, let me check again. Wait, when I wrote down the digits, starting from the right:\n\nFirst digit (units): 8\n\nSecond (tens): 2\n\nThird (hundreds): 4\n\nFourth (thousands): 4\n\nFifth (ten thousands): 4\n\nSixth (hundred thousands): 5\n\nSeventh (millions): 8\n\nEighth (ten millions): 2\n\nNinth (hundred millions): 9\n\nSo the number is 92,544,6428? Wait, but commas are usually placed every three digits. So starting from the right, every three digits. So the digits are:\n\n9 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (units). Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the order.\n\nWait, when adding, we start from the rightmost digit (units), which is the ninth digit from the left. So the digits in order from left to right (billions to hundred millions):\n\nHundred millions: 9\n\nTen millions: 2\n\nMillions: 5\n\nHundred thousands: 4\n\nTen thousands: 4\n\nThousands: 4\n\nHundreds: 2\n\nTens: 8\n\nUnits: 8\n\nSo the number is 92,544,6428? Wait, but that would be 92,544,6428. Wait, but 92,544,6428 is 92,544,6428. Wait, but let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the order. Let me reconstruct the sum step by step.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\nPosition 1 (units): 4 + 4 = 8\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 write 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5 \u2192 write 5, carry 0\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I messed up the carryover steps. Let me redo the addition with proper tracking.\n\nLet me create a table:\n\nPosition | First Number | Second Number | Sum\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nUnits (10^0) | 4 | 4 | 8\nTens (10^1) | 7 | 5 | 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\nHundreds (10^2) | 1 | 3 | 4\nThousands (10^3) | 8 | 6 | 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\nTen thousands (10^4) | 7 | 7 | 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\nHundred thousands (10^5) | 7 | 8 | 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\nMillions (10^6) | 8 | 3 | 8\nTen millions (10^7) | 5 | 3 | 8\nHundred millions (10^8) | 5 | 3 | 9\n\nWait, so the sum is 9 (hundred millions) 2 (ten millions) 5 (millions) 4 (hundred thousands) 4 (ten thousands) 4 (thousands) 2 (hundreds) 8 (tens) 8 (units). So the number is 92,544,6428. Wait, but 92,544,6428. Let me check if that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should use another method. Let me add the numbers step by step.\n\nFirst, 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354.\n\nLet me break them down:\n\n57,787,8174 = 50,000,0000 + 7,000,0000 + 700,000 + 80,000 + 7,000 + 800 + 10 + 7 + 4\n\n35,876,1354 = 30,000,0000 + 5,000,0000 + 800,000 + 70,000 + 6,000 + 100 + 30 + 5 + 4\n\nAdding these together:\n\n50,000,0000 + 30,000,0000 = 80,000,0000\n\n7,000,0000 + 5,000,0000 = 12,000,0000\n\n700,000 + 800,000 = 1,500,000\n\n80,000 + 70,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 6,000 = 13,000\n\n800 + 100 = 900\n\n10 + 30 = 40\n\n7 + 5 = 12\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\nNow add all these:\n\n80,000,0000 + 12,000,0000 = 92,000,0000\n\n92,000,0000 + 1,500,000 = 93,500,0000\n\n93,500,0000 + 150,000 = 93,650,0000\n\n93,650,0000 + 13,000 = 93,663,0000\n\n93,663,0000 + 900 = 93,663,9000\n\n93,663,9000 + 40 = 93,663,9400\n\n93,663,9400 + 12 = 93,663,9512\n\n93,663,9512 + 8 = 93,663,9520\n\nWait, but this seems conflicting with the previous result. Wait, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, breaking down the numbers:\n\nFirst number: 57,787,8174\n\n50,000,0000 + 7,000,0000 = 57,000,0000\n\n700,000 + 800,000 = 1,500,000\n\n80,000 + 70,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 6,000 = 13,000\n\n800 + 100 = 900\n\n10 + 30 = 40\n\n7 + 5 = 12\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\nSo adding all these components:\n\n57,000,0000 + 7,000,0000 = 64,000,0000\n\nWait, no, 57,000,0000 + 7,000,0000 is 64,000,0000?\n\nWait, 57 million plus 7 million is 64 million. Yes.\n\nThen 1,500,000 + 150,000 = 1,650,000\n\nThen 13,000 + 900 = 13,900\n\nThen 40 + 12 = 52\n\nThen 52 + 8 = 60\n\nSo total is 64,000,0000 + 1,650,000 = 65,650,0000\n\n65,650,0000 + 13,900 = 65,663,9000\n\n65,663,9000 + 52 = 65,663,9552\n\n65,663,9552 + 60 = 65,663,9562\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Maybe this method isn't the best. Let me try adding the two numbers directly.\n\nLet me write them down:\n\n      57,787,8174\n    + 35,876,1354\n    -------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n7 + 5 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5\n\n8 + 6 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\n7 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\n7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16 (write 6, carry 1)\n\n5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\n3 + 0 (since the second number has no more digits) = 3\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I need to check again.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step with proper alignment:\n\nFirst number: 5 7 7 8 7 8 1 7 4\n\nSecond number: 3 5 8 7 6 1 3 5 4\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n          5 7 7 8 7 8 1 7 4\n\n        + 3 5 8 7 6 1 3 5 4\n\n        ---------------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n4 + 4 = 8. Write 8.\n\nNext digit (tens place):\n\n7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundreds place):\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5. Write 5, carry 0.\n\nNext (thousands place):\n\n8 + 6 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten thousands place):\n\n7 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundred thousands place):\n\n7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nNext (millions place):\n\n5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, carry 0.\n\nNext (ten millions place):\n\n3 + 0 (since the second number has no more digits) = 3. Write 3, carry 0.\n\nFinally, the hundred millions place:\n\n5 + 3 = 8. Write 8.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:\n\n8 (units), 2 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 4 (thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 6 (hundred thousands), 9 (millions), 3 (ten millions), 8 (hundred millions).\n\nSo the sum is 8 3 9 6 5 4 5 2 8. Wait, no, wait. Wait, when we write the digits from left to right, it's:\n\nHundred millions: 8\n\nTen millions: 3\n\nMillions: 9\n\nHundred thousands: 6\n\nTen thousands: 5\n\nThousands: 4\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 2\n\nUnits: 8\n\nSo the number is 83,965,4528? Wait, but commas are every three digits. So 83,965,4528 would be 83,965,4528. Wait, but 83 million, 965 thousand, 4528. But that seems too high. Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the carryover steps. Let me go through each column again:\n\nStarting from the right (units):\n\n4 + 4 = 8. Correct.\n\nTens place:\n\n7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundreds place:\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5. Correct.\n\nThousands place:\n\n8 + 6 = 14. Write 4, carry 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place:\n\n7 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 15. Write 5, carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands place:\n\n7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1. Correct.\n\nMillions place:\n\n5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, carry 0. Correct.\n\nTen millions place:\n\n3 + 0 (since the second number has no more digits) = 3. Write 3. Correct.\n\nHundred millions place:\n\n5 + 3 = 8. Write 8. Correct.\n\nSo the digits from left to right (hundred millions to units):\n\n8 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units). So the number is 83,965,4528. Wait, but 83,965,4528. Let me check if that's the case.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should use another method. Let me add the numbers using column addition with proper tracking.\n\nFirst, write both numbers:\n\n57,787,8174\n\n+35,876,1354\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n          57,787,8174\n\n        + 35,876,1354\n\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n4 + 4 = 8. Write 8.\n\n7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5. Write 5, carry 0.\n\n8 + 6 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\n7 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\n7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\n5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, carry 0.\n\n3 + 0 (since there are no more digits in the second number) = 3. Write 3, carry 0.\n\n5 + 3 = 8. Write 8.\n\nSo the result is 83,965,4528. Wait, but 83,965,4528. Let me check if that's correct by another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the fact that 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354 = ?\n\nLet me add 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354.\n\nFirst, add 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354.\n\nLet me add the two numbers:\n\n57,787,8174\n\n+35,876,1354\n\nStart adding from the right:\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n7 + 5 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n1 + 3 + 1 = 5\n\n8 + 6 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\n7 + 7 + 1 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\n7 + 8 + 1 = 16 (write 6, carry 1)\n\n5 + 3 + 1 = 9\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n5 + 3 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 83,965,4528. Wait, but 83,965,4528. Let me check if this is correct by using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard addition algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write the numbers:\n\n      57,787,8174\n\n    + 35,876,1354\n\nStart adding from the right:\n\nUnits place: 4 + 4 = 8. Write 8.\n\nTens place: 7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 5. Write 5, carry 0.\n\nThousands place: 8 + 6 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 7 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: 5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, carry 0.\n\nTen millions place: 3 + 0 = 3. Write 3, carry 0.\n\nHundred millions place: 5 + 3 = 8. Write 8.\n\nSo the sum is 83,965,4528. Wait, but 83,965,4528. Let me check if this is correct by using a calculator-like approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the fact that 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354 = ?\n\nLet me compute 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354.\n\nFirst, add 57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354.\n\nLet me break it down:\n\n57,787,8174 = 50,000,0000 + 7,000,0000 + 700,000 + 80,000 + 7,000 + 800 + 10 + 7 + 4\n\n35,876,1354 = 30,000,0000 + 5,000,0000 + 800,000 + 70,000 + 6,000 + 100 + 30 + 5 + 4\n\nAdding these components:\n\n50,000,0000 + 30,000,0000 = 80,000,0000\n\n7,000,0000 + 5,000,0000 = 12,000,0000\n\n700,000 + 800,000 = 1,500,000\n\n80,000 + 70,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 6,000 = 13,000\n\n800 + 100 = 900\n\n10 + 30 = 40\n\n7 + 5 = 12\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\nNow, adding all these together:\n\n80,000,0000 + 12,000,0000 = 92,000,0000\n\n92,000,0000 + 1,500,000 = 93,500,0000\n\n93,500,0000 + 150,000 = 93,650,0000\n\n93,650,0000 + 13,000 = 93,663,0000\n\n93,663,0000 + 900 = 93,663,9000\n\n93,663,9000 + 40 = 93,663,9400\n\n93,663,9400 + 12 = 93,663,9512\n\n93,663,9512 + 8 = 93,663,9520\n\nWait, this is conflicting with the previous result. So according to this method, the sum is 93,663,9520. But according to the vertical addition, it's 83,965,4528. These two results are different. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, let me check the breakdown again. The first number is 57,787,8174. So:\n\n50,000,0000 (50 million)\n\n7,000,0000 (7 million)\n\n700,000 (700 thousand)\n\n80,000 (80 thousand)\n\n7,000 (7 thousand)\n\n800 (800)\n\n10 (10)\n\n7 (7)\n\n4 (4)\n\nSecond number: 35,876,1354\n\n30,000,0000 (30 million)\n\n5,000,0000 (5 million)\n\n800,000 (800 thousand)\n\n70,000 (70 thousand)\n\n6,000 (6 thousand)\n\n100 (100)\n\n30 (30)\n\n5 (5)\n\n4 (4)\n\nAdding these components:\n\n50,000,0000 + 30,000,0000 = 80,000,0000\n\n7,000,0000 + 5,000,0000 = 12,000,0000\n\n700,000 + 800,000 = 1,500,000\n\n80,000 + 70,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 6,000 = 13,000\n\n800 + 100 = 900\n\n10 + 30 = 40\n\n7 + 5 = 12\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\nNow adding all these:\n\n80,000,0000 + 12,000,0000 = 92,000,0000\n\n92,000,0000 + 1,500,000 = 93,500,0000\n\n93,500,0000 + 150,000 = 93,650,0000\n\n93,650,0000 + 13,000 = 93,663,0000\n\n93,663,0000 + 900 = 93,663,9000\n\n93,663,9000 + 40 = 93,663,9400\n\n93,663,9400 + 12 = 93,663,9512\n\n93,663,9512 + 8 = 93,663,9520\n\nBut according to the vertical addition, the sum is 83,965,4528. Wait, 83,965,4528 is 83,965,4528. Let me convert both numbers to numbers and add them:\n\nFirst number: 57,787,8174\n\nSecond number: 35,876,1354\n\nAdding them:\n\n57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\n57,787,8174 + 35,876,1354\n\n= (57,000,0000 + 35,000,0000) + (787,8174 + 876,1354)\n\n= 92,000,0000 + (787,8174 + 876,1354)\n\nCompute 787,8174 + 876,1354:\n\n787,8174 + 876,1354\n\n= (700,000 + 800,000) + (80,000 + 70,000) + (174 + 1354)\n\nWait, no, better to add directly:\n\n787,8174\n\n+876,1354\n\nStart adding:\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n7 + 5 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n1 + 3 + 1 = 5\n\n8 + 6 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\n7 + 7 + 1 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\n8 + 8 + 1 = 17 (write 7, carry 1)\n\n0 + 0 + 1 = 1\n\nWait, but wait, the numbers are 787,8174 and 876,1354.\n\nWait, let's align them properly:\n\n      787,8174\n\n    + 876,1354\n\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n7 + 5 = 12 (write 2, carry 1)\n\n1 + 3 + 1 = 5\n\n8 + 6 = 14 (write 4, carry 1)\n\n7 + 7 + 1 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\n8 + 8 + 1 = 17 (write 7, carry 1)\n\n0 + 0 + 1 = 1\n\nSo the sum is 1,755,  (wait, let's see):\n\nWait, starting from the right:\n\nUnits: 8\n\nTens: 2\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nThousands: 4\n\nTen thousands: 5\n\nHundred thousands: 7\n\nMillions: 1\n\nTen millions: 7\n\nHundred millions: 1\n\nWait, no, let me write the digits:\n\nFro