n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition1:5\n\nWait, no. Wait, when adding, the first digit added (ones place) is position9, which became 0. Then position8 became 5, position7 became 9, position6 became 4, position5 became 2, position4 became 6, position3 became 4, position2 became 5, position1 became 5. So the number is 5 (hundred-millions), 5 (ten-millions), 0 (millions), 2 (hundred-thousands), 6 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, that can't be right. Wait, no. Wait, the positions are as follows:\n\nPosition1: hundred-millions\n\nPosition2: ten-millions\n\nPosition3: millions\n\nPosition4: hundred-thousands\n\nPosition5: ten-thousands\n\nPosition6: thousands\n\nPosition7: hundreds\n\nPosition8: tens\n\nPosition9: ones\n\nSo the digits added are:\n\nPosition9:0\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition7:9\n\nPosition6:4\n\nPosition5:2\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition1:5\n\nSo the number is:\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition2:5\n\nPosition3:4\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition5:2\n\nPosition6:4\n\nPosition7:9\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition9:0\n\nWait, that would be 5,502,644,50? No, that doesn't make sense. Wait, no. Wait, the positions are from right to left. Wait, no, when we added the digits starting from the right, the first digit we added (ones place) became the rightmost digit in the sum. So the order of digits in the sum is:\n\nPosition9 (ones):0\n\nPosition8 (tens):5\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):9\n\nPosition6 (thousands):4\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):6\n\nPosition3 (millions):4\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):5\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):5\n\nSo the number is 5 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). So written out: 5,544,624,950. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 5 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0