ousands:2 +9=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nTen-thousands:3 +0=3 +1=4, carry0\n\nHundred-thousands:7 +5=12 \u21922, carry1\n\nMillions:4 +4=8 +1=9, carry0\n\nTen-millions:4 +2=6 +0=6 (since second number's ten millions place is 2)\n\nWait, wait, the second number is 24,509,737, which is 024,509,737. So:\n\nTen millions place:2\n\nMillions place:4\n\nHundred thousands place:5\n\nTen thousands place:0\n\nThousands place:9\n\nHundreds place:7\n\nTens place:3\n\nOnes place:7\n\nSo when adding ten millions place:4 (from first number) +2 (from second number) =6, no carryover.\n\nWait, previously, I thought the second number's ten millions place is 2, so adding 4 +2=6. But in the previous digit-by-digit addition, I incorrectly took the second number's ten millions place as 2, but in the first number, ten millions place is 4. So let's correct that.\n\nLet me redo the digit-by-digit addition correctly:\n\nFirst number:947,732,858\n\nDigits:\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:4\n\nMillions:7\n\nHundred thousands:7\n\nTen thousands:3\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:8\n\nSecond number:24,509,737\n\nDigits:\n\nHundred millions:0\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:0\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:7\n\nTens:3\n\nOnes:7\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1. Ones:8 +7=15 \u21925, carry1\n\n2. Tens:5 +3=8 +1=9, carry0\n\n3. Hundreds:8 +7=15 \u21925, carry1\n\n4. Thousands:2 +9=11 \u21921, carry1\n\n5. Ten-thousands:3 +0=3 +1=4, carry0\n\n6. Hundred-thousands:7 +5=12 \u21922, carry1\n\n7. Millions:4 +4=8 +1=9, carry0\n\n8. Ten-millions:4 +2=6 +0=6, carry0\n\n9. Hundred-millions:9 +0=9 +0=9, carry0\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo the sum is 969,241,595.\n\nWait, but 947,732,858 +24,509,737 should be 972,242,595. But according to this digit-by-digit addition, it's 969,241,595. Still not matching. So there's a mistake here.\n\nWait, let's compute 947,732,858 +24,509,737 manually:\n\n947,732,858 +24,509,737\n\n= (900,000,000 +47,732,858) + (20,000,000 +4,509,737)\n\n= 900,000,000 +20,000,000 +47,732,858 +4,509,737\n\n= 920,000,000 +52,242,595\n\n= 972,242,595.\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 969,241,595. So there's a discrepancy of 3,001,000. What's wrong here?\n\nWait, let's check the digit-by-digit addition again.\n\nFirst number:947,732,858\n\nDigits:\n\n9 (hundred millions)\n\n4 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n7 (hundred thousands)\n\n3 (ten thousands)\n\n2 (thousands)\n\n8 (hundreds)\n\n5 (tens)\n\n8 (ones)\n\nSecond number:24,509,737\n\nDigits:\n\n0 (hundred millions)\n\n2 (ten millions)\n\n4 (millions)\n\n5 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n9 (thousands)\n\n7 (hundreds)\n\n3 (tens)\n\n7 (ones)\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1. Ones:8 +7=15 \u21925, carry1\n\n2. Tens:5 +3=8 +1=9, carry0\n\n3. Hundreds:8 +7=15 \u21925, carry1\n\n4. Thousands:2 +9=11 \u21921, carry1\n\n5. Ten-thousands:3 +0=3 +1=4, carry0\n\n6. Hundred-thousands:7 +5=12 \u21922, carry1\n\n7. Millions:4 +4=8 +1=9, carry0\n\n8. Ten-millions:4 +2=6 +0=6, carry0\n\n9. Hundred-millions:9 +0=9 +0=9, carry0\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred millions:9\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:2\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:5\n\nSo the number is 969,241,595.\n\nBut the correct sum is 972,242,595. So the difference is 972,242,595 -969,241,595=3,001,000.\n\nWait, so where is the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait, in the ten-millions place. The first number's ten millions digit is 4, and the second number's ten millions digit is 2. So 4 +2=6. But in the digit-by-digit addition, we have 4 (from first number) +2 (from second number) =6, which is correct. Then, the millions place:7 (from first number) +4 (from second number)=11 \u21921, carry1. Wait, but in the digit-by-digit addition, we have:\n\nMillions place:7 (fir