units to hundred millions):\n\n6, 5, 5, 0, 1, 0, 5, 1, 6, 5\n\nBut when writing the number, we need to reverse this order to get the correct place values. Wait, no. Wait, actually, when you add numbers, the digits are added starting from the right, so the sum is written in the order of the digits as they are computed. So the first digit computed is the units, then tens, hundreds, etc., so the number is written starting from the units digit. But when you write the number, you have to write it left to right, so the first digit you get is the units, then tens, etc., so the number is 6,5,5,0,1,0,5,1,6,5. But this is not correct. Wait, no. Wait, the digits are:\n\n6 (units)\n\n5 (tens)\n\n5 (hundreds)\n\n0 (thousands)\n\n1 (ten thousands)\n\n0 (hundred thousands)\n\n5 (millions)\n\n1 (ten millions)\n\n6 (hundred millions)\n\n5 (billions)\n\nSo the number is 5,610,501,0556. But this is incorrect. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe I need to use a different method. Let's use the fact that 248,708,728 + 378,220,428 can be written as:\n\n248,708,728 = 200,000,000 + 48,708,728\n\n378,220,428 = 300,000,000 + 78,220,428\n\nAdding these together:\n\n200,000,000 + 300,000,000 = 500,000,000\n\n48,708,728 + 78,220,428 = ?\n\nLet's compute 48,708,728 + 78,220,428:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n2 + 2 = 4 + 1 = 5, carry 0\n\n7 + 4 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1, carry 0\n\n8 + 2 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\n0 + 2 = 2 + 1 = 3, carry 0\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n4 + 0 = 4 + 1 = 5, carry 0\n\nWait, but the digits of 48,708,728 are:\n\n4 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units)\n\nAnd 78,220,428 are:\n\n7 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units)\n\nAdding these:\n\nUnits:8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nTens:2 + 2 = 4 + 1 = 5, carry 0\n\nHundreds