= 10 + 1 = 11. Write 11.\n\nSo the sum is 11,108,200. Wait, but 11,108,200 is 11 million 108 thousand 200. But 483 million + 627 million is 1,110 million. So 1,110,000,000. But according to vertical addition, it's 11,108,200. That's a factor of 1000 difference. So something is wrong here.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, the numbers are 483,277,968 and 627,002,452.\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n      483,277,968\n\n    + 627,002,452\n\n------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n8 + 2 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext digit (tens): 6 + 5 = 11 + 1 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundreds): 9 + 4 = 13 + 1 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nNext (thousands): 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten thousands): 7 + 0 = 7 + 1 = 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nNext (hundred thousands): 2 + 0 = 2. Write 2.\n\nNext (millions): 3 + 7 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten millions): 8 + 2 = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundred millions): 4 + 6 = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 11.\n\nSo the sum is 11,108,200. But 483,277,968 + 627,002,452 should be 1,110,300,420. Wait, no. Wait, 483,277,968 + 627,002,452.\n\nWait, 483,277,968 + 627,002,452.\n\nLet me compute this as:\n\n483,277,968\n\n+627,002,452\n\n= (400,000,000 + 600,000,000) + (80,000,000 + 20,000,000) + (3,000,000 + 7,000,000) + (200,000 + 0) + (70,000 + 2,000) + (7,000 + 400) + (900 + 50) + (60 + 2) + (8 + 2)\n\n= 1,000,000,000 + 100,000,000 + 10,000,000 + 200,000 + 72,000 + 9,400 + 750 + 62 + 10\n\n= 1,000,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 1,100,000,000\n\n1,100,000,000 + 10,000,000 = 1,110,000,000\n\n1,110,000,000 + 200,000 = 1,110,200,000\n\n1,110,200,000 + 72,000 = 1,110,272,000\n\n1,110,272,000 + 9,400 = 1,110,272,940\n\n1,110,272,940 + 750 = 1,110,273,690\n\n1,110,273,690 + 62 = 1,110,273,752\n\n1,110,273,752 + 10 = 1,110,273,762\n\nBut according to vertical addition, it's 11,108,200. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a