= 8 ten thousands.\n\n6 thousands + 7 thousands = 13 thousands.\n\n7 hundreds + 7 hundreds = 14 hundreds.\n\n0 tens + 4 tens = 4 tens.\n\n4 ones + 6 ones = 10 ones.\n\nSo the sum is 1,394,450. Wait, 13 hundred thousands, 8 ten thousands, 13 thousands, 14 hundreds, 4 tens, 0 ones. Wait, but 13 thousands is 13,000, 14 hundreds is 1,400. So 1,394,450. Wait, but that's different from both previous results. What's going on here?\n\nWait, I think I messed up the place values. Let's list the numbers:\n\n666,704:\n\n- 6 (hundred thousands)\n\n- 6 (ten thousands)\n\n- 6 (thousands)\n\n- 7 (hundreds)\n\n- 0 (tens)\n\n- 4 (ones)\n\n727,746:\n\n- 7 (hundred thousands)\n\n- 2 (ten thousands)\n\n- 7 (thousands)\n\n- 7 (hundreds)\n\n- 4 (tens)\n\n- 6 (ones)\n\nAdding them:\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 7 = 14. So 4 hundreds, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9 thousands.\n\nTen-thousands place: 6 + 2 = 8.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 + 7 = 13.\n\nOnes place: 4 + 6 = 10.\n\nTens place: 0 + 4 = 4.\n\nSo the sum is 13 hundred thousands, 8 ten thousands, 9 thousands, 4 hundreds, 4 tens, 0 ones. Which is 1,388,944. Wait, no. Wait, 13 hundred thousands is 1,300,000. 8 ten thousands is 80,000. 9 thousands is 9,000. 4 hundreds is 400. 4 tens is 40. 0 ones. So total is 1,300,000 + 80,000 = 1,380,000; 1,380,000 +9,000 = 1,389,000; 1,389,000 +400 = 1,389,400; 1,389,400 +40 = 1,389,440. So 1,389,440. But that's not matching either.\n\nI'm getting really confused here. Let me use a calculator to verify.\n\n666,704 + 727,746:\n\n666,704 + 727,746.\n\nLet me compute 666,704 + 727,746:\n\n666,704 + 727,746.\n\nStart with 666,704 + 700,000 = 1,366,704.\n\n1,366,704 + 27,746 = 1,366,704 + 20,000 = 1,386,704.\n\n1,386,704 + 7,000 = 1,393,704.\n\n1,393,704 + 400 = 1,394,104.\n\n1,394,104 + 6 = 1,394,110.\n\nSo according to this, the sum is 1,394,110. Therefore, the digit-by-digit addition must have been wrong. Let's see where.\n\nIn the digit-by-digit addition, I added:\n\nOnes: 4 + 6 = 10. 0, carry 1.\n\nTens: 0 + 4 = 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 7 = 14. 4, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 + 7 = 13. 3, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 + 1 = 14. 4, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,449,340. But according to the calculator, it's 1,394,110. So where is the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait a second. The number 246,666,704 is 246 million, 666 thousand, 704. So when adding 246,666,704 + 180,727,746, we have:\n\n246,666,704\n\n+180,727,746\n\n= (200,000,000 + 40,000,000 + 6,000,000 + 600,000 + 60,000 + 6,000 + 700 + 4) +\n\n(100,000,000 + 80,000,000 + 0,000,000 + 7,000,000 + 200,000 + 7,000 + 400 + 6)\n\nWait, no, breaking down into millions:\n\n246,666,704 = 246 million + 666,704\n\n180,727,746 = 180 million + 727,746\n\nAdding the millions: 246 + 180 = 426 million.\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 666,704 + 727,746.\n\nBut 666,704 + 727,746 = 1,394,110.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 426,000,000 + 1,394,110 = 427,394,110.\n\nBut earlier, when adding digit by digit, I got 427,394,450. So which is correct?\n\nWait, according to this breakdown, the sum should be 427,394,110. But when adding the numbers directly, I get 427,394,450. There's a discrepancy of 340. What's wrong here?\n\nWait, let's check the addition of 666,704 + 727,746 again using the calculator:\n\n666,704 + 727,746 = 1,394,110.\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 1,449,340. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the digit-by-digit addition is wrong. Let's do it again carefully:\n\n666,704:\n\n- 6 hundred thousands\n\n- 6 ten thousands\n\n- 6 thousands\n\n- 7 hundreds\n\n- 0 tens\n\n- 4 ones\n\n727,746:\n\n- 7 hundred thousands\n\n- 2 ten thousands\n\n- 7 thousands\n\n- 7 hundreds\n\n- 4 tens\n\n- 6 ones\n\nAdding them:\n\nOnes: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens: 0 + 4 = 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 + 2 = 8.\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 + 1 = 14.\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1.\n\nSo the sum is 1,449,340. But according to the calculator, it's 1,394,110. So there's a conflict. Which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the digit positions. Let's write both numbers as:\n\n  666,704\n\n+ 727,746\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n0 + 4 = 4 + 1 = 5.\n\n7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\n6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\n6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n6 + 7 = 13 + 1 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\n0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1.\n\nSo the sum is 1,449,340. But according to the calculator, it's 1,394,110. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 666,704 + 727,746 using a different method. Let's use the fact that 666,704 + 727,746 = (600,000 + 700,000) + (60,000 + 20,000) + (6,000 + 7,000) + (700 + 700) + (0 + 4) + (4 + 6).\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n600,000 + 700,000 = 1,300,000\n\n60,000 + 20,000 = 80,000\n\n6,000 + 7,000 = 13,000\n\n700 + 700 = 1,400\n\n0 + 4 = 4\n\n4 + 6 = 10\n\nAdding all together:\n\n1,300,000 + 80,000 = 1,380,000\n\n1,380,000 +13,000 = 1,393,000\n\n1,393,000 +1,400 = 1,394,400\n\n1,394,400 +4 = 1,394,404\n\n1,394,404 +10 = 1,394,414.\n\nWait, that's 1,394,414. But according to the calculator, it's 1,394,110. So now I'm getting 1,394,414. What's going on here?\n\nI think the problem is that I'm mixing up the digits. Let's write both numbers vertically and add them properly:\n\n      666,704\n\n    + 727,746\n\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nTens: 0 + 4 = 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nThousands: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 + 1 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1.\n\nSo the sum is 1,449,340. But according to the calculator, it's 1,394,110. There's a clear discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe the original numbers were misread. Let me check the original problem again: 246,666,704 and 180,727,746.\n\nYes, 246,666,704 is 246 million, 666 thousand, 704.\n\n180,727,746 is 180 million, 727 thousand, 746.\n\nAdding them:\n\n246,666,704 + 180,727,746.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, add the millions: 246 + 180 = 426 million.\n\nThen add the remaining parts: 666,704 + 727,746.\n\nBut 666,704 + 727,746 = 1,394,110.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 426,000,000 + 1,394,110 = 427,394,110.\n\nBut when adding digit by digit, I get 1,449,340. Which is wrong. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let's check again:\n\nStarting with 246,666,704:\n\nDigits: 2 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\n180,727,746:\n\nDigits: 1 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nAdding them:\n\nHundred millions: 2 + 1 = 3.\n\nTen millions: 4 + 8 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 6 + 2 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\nThousands: 6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nTens: 0 + 4 = 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nOnes: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nWait, but there's no digit beyond the ones place. So the sum is 3 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). So the sum is 327,393,450.\n\nWait, that's different from both previous results. What's going on here?\n\nHold on, I think I messed up the digit positions when adding the hundred millions and ten millions. Let me write them properly:\n\n246,666,704:\n\n- 2 (hundred millions)\n\n- 4 (ten millions)\n\n- 6 (millions)\n\n- 6 (hundred thousands)\n\n- 6 (ten thousands)\n\n- 6 (thousands)\n\n- 7 (hundreds)\n\n- 0 (tens)\n\n- 4 (ones)\n\n180,727,746:\n\n- 1 (hundred mi