\n31,0277 +300,000 =331,0277\n\n331,0277 +48,6610 =331,0277 +40,000 =335,0277\n\n335,0277 +8,6610 =335,0277 +8,000 =335,0377\n\n335,0377 +6610 =335,0377 +6,000 =335,0477\n\n335,0477 +610 =335,0477 +600 =335,0577\n\n335,0577 +10 =335,0587\n\nWait, that's 335,0587. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 380,6887. There's a discrepancy here. What's wrong?\n\nAh, I see. When adding 031,0277 (which is 31,0277) and 348,6610, we need to align the digits properly. Let's write them as 7-digit numbers:\n\n031,0277 \u2192 0 3 1 0 2 7 7\n\n348,6610 \u21923 4 8 6 6 1 0\n\nAdding:\n\nPosition 1:7 +0=7\n\nPosition 2:7 +1=8\n\nPosition 3:2 +6=8\n\nPosition 4:0 +8=8\n\nPosition 5:1 +6=7\n\nPosition 6:3 +3=6\n\nPosition 7:0 +0=0\n\nSo the sum is 0 3 1 0 2 7 7 +3 4 8 6 6 1 0 = 3 8 0 6 8 8 7 \u2192 380,6887. But when adding the numbers as 31,0277 +348,6610, we get 335,0587. There's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 31,0277 +348,6610 directly.\n\n31,0277 +348,6610:\n\n31,0277 +300,000 =331,0277\n\n331,0277 +48,6610 =331,0277 +40,000 =335,0277\n\n335,0277 +8,6610 =335,0277 +8,000 =335,0377\n\n335,0377 +6610 =335,0377 +6,000 =335,0477\n\n335,0477 +610 =335,0477 +600 =335,0577\n\n335,0577 +10 =335,0587\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 380,6887. There's a problem here. Which is correct?\n\nWait, 31,0277 is 31,0277. 348,6610 is 348,6610. Adding them:\n\n31,0277 +348,6610:\n\n31,0277 +348,6610 = 31,0277 +348,6610.\n\nLet me compute this using another method. Let's compute 31,0277 +348,6610:\n\n31,0277 +348,6610 = (30,000 +1,0277) + (300,000 +48,6610)\n\n=30,000 +1,0277 +300,000 +48,6610\n\n= (30,000 +300,000) + (1,0277 +48,6610)\n\n=330,000 +50, 6887\n\nWait, 1,0277 +48,6610 =49,6887\n\nSo total is 330,000 +49,6887 =379,6887\n\nWait, 330,000 +49,6887 =379,6887. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 380,6887. There's a discrepancy of 1,000.\n\nWait, what's 1,0277 +48,6610?\n\n1,0277 +48,6610 =49,6887. Yes. Then 330,000 +