out commas, it's 872662112. So that's 87,266,2112. Wait, but 87,266,2112 would be 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. But 87 million is 87,000,000, 266 thousand is 266,000, and 2112 is 2,112. So adding those together: 87,000,000 + 266,000 = 87,266,000. Then 87,266,000 + 2,112 = 87,268,112. But the number written is 872662112. Let me check if that's 87,266,2112. Wait, 87,266,2112 would be 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. But 87,266,2112 is 87,266,2112. Wait, maybe the commas are misplaced. Alternatively, maybe the number is 87,266,2112, which is 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. But when written without commas, it's 872662112. Let me check the digits:\n\n8 7 2 6 6 2 1 1 2. So starting from the left: 8 (ten millions place?), 7 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones), 2. Wait, that's 9 digits. So 87,266,2112 is 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. But when written as 872662112, that's 87,266,2112. So the commas are every three digits starting from the right. So 872662112 is 87,266,2112. So that's correct.\n\nSimilarly, the second number is 91,362,7987. Let's parse that. 91,362,7987. Breaking it down: 91 million, 362 thousand, 7987. But written without commas: 913627987. Let's count the digits: 9 1 3 6 2 7 9 8 7. That's 9 digits. So 91,362,7987 is 91 million, 362 thousand, 7987. But written as 913627987, which is 91,362,7987. So the second number is 91,362,7987.\n\nSo now, we need to add 87,266,2112 and 91,362,7987. Let me write them down aligned properly:\n\n          87,266,2112\n        + 91,362,7987\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the ones place):\n\nDigits: 2 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 9. So the ones digit is 9.\n\nNext, the tens place: 1 + 8 = 9. So tens digit is 9.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 9 = 10. So we write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 2 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 10. Again, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 6 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 9. So 9, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 + 6 = 12. Write down 2, carry over 1.\n\nMillions place: 7 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nTen millions place: 8 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 18. Write down 8, carry over 1.\n\nHundred millions place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1.\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right:\n\nOnes: 9\n\nTens: 9\n\nHundreds: 0\n\nThousands: 0\n\nTen thousands: 9\n\nHundred thousands: 2\n\nMillions: 1\n\nTen millions: 8\n\nHundred millions: 1\n\nSo the sum is 188,632,909.\n\nWait, let me verify that step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nFirst, let's write both numbers with the commas properly:\n\nFirst number: 87,266,2112\n\nSecond number: 91,362,7987\n\nLet me write them vertically aligned:\n\n          87,266,2112\n        + 91,362,7987\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n2 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 9. Write 9.\n\nNext digit (tens place):\n\n1 (from first number) + 8 (from second number) = 9. Write 9.\n\nNext (hundreds place):\n\n1 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext (thousands place):\n\n2 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten thousands place):\n\n6 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9.\n\nNext (hundred thousands place):\n\n6 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nNext (millions place):\n\n7 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten millions place):\n\n8 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 18. Write 8, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundred millions place):\n\n0 (since first number has no hundred millions) + 0 (second number has no hundred millions) + 1 (carry) = 1. Write 1.\n\nSo the result is 188,632,909.\n\nWait, let me check if that makes sense. Let's do the addition another way to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, we can add the two numbers as they are:\n\n87,266,2112\n\n+91,362,7987\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 2 + 1 = 9\n\n6 + 6 = 12 (carry 1)\n\n7 + 3 + 1 = 11 (carry 1)\n\n8 + 9 + 1 = 18 (carry 1)\n\n0 + 0 + 1 = 1\n\nSo the sum is 188,632,909. That seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\n87,266,2112 + 91,362,7987.\n\nLet me split 91,362,7987 into 90,000,0000 and 1,362,7987.\n\nSo 87,266,2112 + 90,000,0000 = 177,266,2112\n\nThen 177,266,2112 + 1,362,7987.\n\nLet's add those two:\n\n177,266,2112\n\n+ 1,362,7987\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 2 + 1 = 9\n\n6 + 7 = 13 (carry 1)\n\n7 + 3 + 1 = 11 (carry 1)\n\n1 + 1 + 1 = 3\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, let's align them properly:\n\n177,266,2112\n\n+    1,362,7987\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n          177,266,2112\n        +     1,362,7987\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 2 + 1 = 9\n\n6 + 7 = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\n7 + 3 + 1 = 11 (write 1, carry 1)\n\n1 + 1 + 1 = 3\n\n0 + 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1\n\nSo the sum is 188,632,909. Same result. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method. Let's see:\n\n87,266,2112 is 8.72662112 x 10^8\n\n91,362,7987 is 9.13627987 x 10^8\n\nAdding them together: 8.72662112 + 9.13627987 = 17.86290101 x 10^8 = 178,629,010.1. Wait, but that's not matching. Wait, hold on. Wait, 8.72662112 + 9.13627987:\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n8.72662112\n\n+9.13627987\n\n= (8 + 9) + (0.72662112 + 0.13627987)\n\n= 17 + (0.72662112 + 0.13627987)\n\nCompute 0.72662112 + 0.13627987:\n\n0.72662112\n\n+0.13627987\n\n= 0.86290099\n\nSo total is 17.86290099. Then multiply by 10^8: 17.86290099 x 10^8 = 178,629,009.9. But our previous result was 188,632,909. Hmm, there's a discrepancy here. Wait, why is that?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in converting the numbers to scientific notation. Let's check:\n\nFirst number: 87,266,2112. Let's parse this as 87,266,2112. If we consider this as 8.72662112 x 10^8? Wait, 87,266,2112 is 87 million, which is 8.7 x 10^8. Wait, 87 million is 8.7 x 10^8. But 87,266,2112 is 87,266,2112. Wait, 87,000,000 is 8.7 x 10^8. Then 266,2112 is 266,2112. Wait, 266,2112 is 266,000 + 2,112 = 268,112. So 87,266,2112 is 87,000,000 + 268,112 = 87,268,112. Similarly, 91,362,7987 is 91,000,000 + 362,7987 = 91,362,7987. So 91,362,7987 is 91,362,7987. So converting to scientific notation:\n\n87,268,112 is 8.7268112 x 10^7\n\n91,362,7987 is 9.13627987 x 10^7\n\nWait, no. Wait, 87,268,112 is 8.7268112 x 10^7? Wait, 87,268,112 is 8.7268112 x 10^7? Wait, 10^7 is 10,000,000. 8.7268112 x 10^7 is 87,268,112. Yes. Similarly, 91,362,7987 is 9.13627987 x 10^7. So adding them:\n\n8.7268112 x 10^7 + 9.13627987 x 10^7 = (8.7268112 + 9.13627987) x 10^7 = 17.86309107 x 10^7 = 178,630,910.7. But our previous result was 188,632,909. Hmm, so there's a discrepancy here. Wait, why?\n\nWait, perhaps my initial conversion was wrong. Let me check:\n\nFirst number: 87,266,2112. Let's parse this as 87,266,2112. If we consider this as 8.72662112 x 10^8, but 8.72662112 x 10^8 is 87,266,2112. Wait, 10^8 is 100,000,000. 8.72662112 x 100,000,000 = 872,662,112. Wait, that's different. Wait, so maybe my mistake was in the placement of the commas. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number: 872662112. Let's parse this without commas: 8 7 2 6 6 2 1 1 2. So that's 9 digits. So 87,266,2112 is 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. But 87,266,2112 is 87,266,2112. Let's convert this to a number:\n\nStarting from the left:\n\n8 (ten millions place)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n6 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n1 (tens)\n\n1 (ones)\n\n2 (ten ones?)\n\nWait, no. Wait, in the number 87,266,2112, the digits are:\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n6 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n1 (tens)\n\n1 (ones)\n\n2 (ten ones? Wait, no. Wait, the last two digits are 1 and 2. So 1 is tens place, 2 is ones place. So the number is 87,266,2112 = 87,266,2112. Let's compute its value:\n\n87,000,000 + 266,000 + 2,112 = 87,000,000 + 266,000 = 87,266,000 + 2,112 = 87,268,112.\n\nSimilarly, the second number 91,362,7987 is 91,362,7987. Let's compute that:\n\n91,000,000 + 362,000 + 7,987 = 91,000,000 + 362,000 = 91,362,000 + 7,987 = 91,369,987.\n\nWait, so the first number is 87,268,112 and the second is 91,369,987. Let's add those:\n\n87,268,112 + 91,369,987.\n\nLet me compute this:\n\n87,268,112\n\n+91,369,987\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n8 + 6 + 1 = 15 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 9 + 1 = 16 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, let's align them properly:\n\n          87,268,112\n\n        + 91,369,987\n\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\n8 + 6 + 1 = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\n6 + 9 + 1 = 16 (write 6, carry 1)\n\n2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 178,638,099. Wait, that's different from the previous results. Wait, now I'm confused. What's going on here?\n\nWait, let's check the addition step by step again.\n\nFirst number: 87,268,112\n\nSecond number: 91,369,987\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n2 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 9\n\n1 (from first number) + 8 (from second number) = 9\n\n1 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n2 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n8 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\n6 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\n2 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 6. Write 6, no carry.\n\n7 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 8. Write 8.\n\nSo the sum is 178,638,099.\n\nWait, but earlier when I added 87,266,2112 and 91,362,7987, I got 188,632,909. Now, when I converted both numbers to 87,268,112 and 91,369,987, adding them gives 178,638,099. There's a discrepancy here. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the original numbers again. The first number is 872662112. Let's parse this without commas: 8 7 2 6 6 2 1 1 2. So that's 87,266,2112. But 87,266,2112 is 87,266,2112. Let's compute that:\n\n87,000,000 + 266,000 + 2,112 = 87,000,000 + 266,000 = 87,266,000 + 2,112 = 87,268,112. Correct.\n\nSecond number: 913627987. Parsing without commas: 9 1 3 6 2 7 9 8 7. So 91,362,7987. Which is 91,000,000 + 362,000 + 7,987 = 91,000,000 + 362,000 = 91,362,000 + 7,987 = 91,369,987. Correct.\n\nSo adding 87,268,112 + 91,369,987:\n\nLet's do it step by step:\n\n87,268,112\n\n+91,369,987\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n8 + 6 + 1 = 15 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 9 + 1 = 16 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 178,638,099.\n\nBut earlier, when I added 87,266,2112 and 91,362,7987, I got 188,632,909. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the original problem again. The user wrote:\n\n\"Please solve the math problem. Question: What is the sum of 872662112 and 913627987?\"\n\nSo the numbers are 87,266,2112 and 91,362,7987. But when written without commas, they are 872662112 and 913627987. Let's verify the sum again.\n\nFirst number: 87,266,2112. Let's write this as 87,266,2112. So 87 million, 266 thousand, 2112. Which is 87,000,000 + 266,000 + 2,112 = 87,268,112.\n\nSecond number: 91,362,7987. Which is 91,000,000 + 362,000 + 7,987 = 91,369,987.\n\nAdding 87,268,112 + 91,369,987:\n\nLet's do this another way. Let's add the millions:\n\n87,000,000 + 91,000,000 = 178,000,000\n\nThen add the remaining parts:\n\n268,112 + 369,987.\n\n268,112 + 369,987:\n\n200,000 + 300,000 = 500,000\n\n68,112 + 69,987:\n\n60,000 + 60,000 = 120,000\n\n8,112 + 9,987:\n\n8,000 + 9,000 = 17,000\n\n112 + 987 = 1,100\n\nSo adding up:\n\n500,000 + 120,000 = 620,000\n\n620,000 + 17,000 = 637,000\n\n637,000 + 1,100 = 638,100\n\nSo total is 178,000,000 + 638,100 = 178,638,100.\n\nWait, but according to this, the sum is 178,638,100. But when I added the numbers digit by digit, I got 178,638,099. There's a difference of 1. Hmm, so which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check the addition step by step again:\n\nFirst number: 87,268,112\n\nSecond number: 91,369,987\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 7 = 9\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\n1 + 9 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 7 + 1 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n8 + 6 + 1 = 15 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 9 + 1 = 16 (carry 1)\n\n2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 178,638,099.\n\nBut when adding the two numbers as 87,268,112 + 91,369,987, breaking into millions and the rest:\n\n87,000,000 + 91,000,000 = 178,000,000\n\n268,112 + 369,987:\n\n268,112 + 369,987:\n\n200,000 + 300,000 = 500,000\n\n68,112 + 69,987:\n\n60,000 + 60,000 = 120,000\n\n8,112 + 9,987:\n\n8,000 + 9,000 = 17,000\n\n112 + 987 = 1,100\n\nTotal: 500,000 + 120,000 = 620,000; 620,000 + 17,000 = 637,000; 637,000 + 1,100 = 638,100.\n\nTotal sum: 178,000,000 + 638,100 = 178,638,100.\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 178,638,099. There's a discrepancy of 1. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, let's check the digit-by-digit addition again:\n\nFirst number: 87,268,112\n\nSecond number: 91,369,987\n\nLet me write them as:\n\n          87,268,112\n\n        + 91,369,987\n\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nPosition 1 (units): 2 + 7 = 9\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 1 + 8 = 9\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 1 + 9 = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 2 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 6 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 13 (write 3, carry 1)\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, in the first number, the digits are:\n\nPosition 1: 2\n\nPosition 2: 1\n\nPosition 3: 1\n\nPosition 4: 2\n\nPosition 5: 6\n\nPosition 6: 6\n\nPosition 7: 2\n\nPosition 8: 1\n\nPosition 9: 8\n\nWait, no. Wait, the first number is 87,268,112. Let's break it down digit by digit:\n\nDigit 1: 8 (ten millions)\n\nDigit 2: 7 (millions)\n\nDigit 3: 2 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit 4: 6 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit 5: 8 (thousands)\n\nDigit 6: 1 (hundreds)\n\nDigit 7: 1 (tens)\n\nDigit 8: 2 (ones)\n\nWait, no. Wait, 87,268,112 is 8 7 2 6 8 1 1 2. Wait, no. Wait, 87,268,112 is 87 million, 268 thousand, 112. So the digits are:\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (thousands)\n\n1 (hundreds)\n\n1 (tens)\n\n2 (ones)\n\nWait, but 87,268,112 is 87,000,000 + 268,000 + 112 = 87,268,112. So the digits are:\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n7 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (thousands)\n\n1 (hundreds)\n\n1 (tens)\n\n2 (ones)\n\nSimilarly, the second number 91,369,987 is 91,000,000 + 369,000 + 987 = 91,369,987. So digits:\n\n9 (ten millions)\n\n1 (millions)\n\n3 (hundred thousands)\n\n6 (ten thousands)\n\n9 (thousands)\n\n9 (hundreds)\n\n8 (tens)\n\n7 (ones)\n\nSo aligning both numbers:\n\n          8 7 2 6 8 1 1 2\n\n        + 9 1 3 6 9 9 8 7\n\n        --------------------\n\nNow, let's perform the addition digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\nPosition 1: 2 + 7 = 9\n\nPosition 2: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nPosition 3: 1 + 9 = 10 (write 0, carry 1)\n\nPosition 4: 8 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 15 (write 5, carry 1)\n\nPosition 5: 6 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 16 (write 6, carry 1)\n\nPosition 6: 2 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 6 (no carry)\n\nPosition 7: 7 + 1 = 8 (no carry)\n\nPosition 8: 8 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 17 (write 7, carry 1). Wait, hold on. Wait, in the first number, the digits are:\n\nPosition 1: 8\n\nPosition 2: 7\n\nPosition 3: 2\n\nPosition 4: 6\n\nPosition 5: 8\n\nPosition 6: 1\n\nPosition 7: 1\n\nPosition 8: 2\n\nWait, no. Wait, the first number is 87,268,112, which is 8 7 2 6 8 1 1 2. So positions 1 to 8:\n\n1:8, 2:7, 3:2, 4:6, 5:8, 6:1, 7:1, 8:2.\n\nSecond number is 91,369,987: 9 1 3 6 9 9 8 7.\n\nSo positions 1 to 8:\n\n1:9, 2:1, 3:3, 4:6, 5:9, 6:9, 7:8, 8:7.\n\nSo adding:\n\nPosition 1: 8 + 9 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nPosition 2: 7 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9, no carry.\n\nPosition 3: 2 + 3 = 5. Write 5, no carry.\n\nPosition 4: 6 + 6 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 5: 8 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 18. Write 8, carry 1.\n\nPosition 6: 1 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nPosition 7: 1 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nPosition 8: 2 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nWait, but we have a carryover at the end, which we didn't account for. So the total sum would be 100,000,000 + ... Wait, no. Wait, the carryover at the end would affect the next digit, but since there are no more digits, we just add it to the existing digits. Wait, but in this case, the carryover at position 8 (the leftmost digit) would actually be added to the hundred millions place. Wait, let's see:\n\nWait, the first number's leftmost digit is 8 (ten millions place), and the second number's leftmost digit is 9 (ten millions place). So adding those gives 8 + 9 = 17. So we write 7 in the hundred millions place and carry over 1 to the next higher place. But since there are no higher places, the carryover becomes the new hundred millions digit. So the total sum would be 1 (hundred millions place) followed by 7 (ten millions place), and then the rest of the digits. Wait, but in our previous digit-by-digit addition, we didn't consider the carryover beyond the leftmost digits. So let's redo the addition with proper tracking of carryovers.\n\nLet me create a table for each digit position, including the carryover:\n\nPosition | Digit1 | Digit2 | Carryover (from previous position)\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n1 | 8 | 9 | 0\n2 | 7 | 1 | 