40,000,000 = 1,740,000,000\n\n+ 10,000,000 = 1,750,000,000\n\n+ 1,000,000 = 1,751,000,000\n\n+ 70,000 = 1,751,070,000\n\n+ 4,074 = 1,751,074,074\n\n+ 0 = 1,751,074,074\n\n+ 13 = 1,751,074,087\n\n+ 12 = 1,751,074,099\n\nWait, that's still different from the vertical addition result of 175,180,712. What's going on here? There's a clear inconsistency. This is confusing. Let me check once more.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me try adding the two numbers directly using another method. Let's use the standard addition algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write the numbers:\n\n          981,574,076\n        + 769,507,636\n        -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n6 + 6 = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n7 + 3 = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n0 + 6 = 6 + 1 = 7. Write 7, no carry.\n\n4 + 7 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n7 + 0 = 7 + 0 = 7. Write 7, no carry.\n\n5 + 5 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n1 + 9 = 10 + 1 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\n8 + 6 = 14 + 1 = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\n9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, write the carried 1 as the next digit.\n\nSo the sum is 175,180,712.\n\nBut according to the component addition, I got 1,751,074,099. Which is 1.75 billion vs 175 million. There's a factor of 10 difference. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the commas in the numbers. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\nThe first number is 981,574,076. Is that 981 million, 574 thousand, 76? Yes. The second number is 769,507,636. That's 769 million, 507 thousand, 636. So when adding, 981 million + 769 million = 1,750 million. Then 574 thousand + 507 thousand = 1,081 thousand. Then 76 + 636 = 752. So total is 1,750,000,000 + 1,081,000 + 752 = 1,751,081,752. Wait, that's different from both previous results. Wait, this is getting more confusing.\n\nWait, let's do the addition step by step without breaking into components:\n\nFirst number: 981,574,076\n\nSecond number: 769,507,636\