ncorrect. Since the vertical addition is the standard method taught in schools, and assuming I did it correctly, the result should be correct. Therefore, the component addition must have an error.\n\nLooking back at the component addition:\n\nFirst number components:\n\n- 900,000,000\n\n- 80,000,000\n\n- 1,000,000\n\n- 500,000\n\n- 70,000\n\n- 4,000\n\n- 0\n\n- 0\n\n- 7\n\n- 6\n\nSecond number components:\n\n- 700,000,000\n\n- 60,000,000\n\n- 9,000,000\n\n- 500,000\n\n- 0\n\n- 0\n\n- 7\n\n- 6\n\n- 3\n\n- 6\n\nAdding each component:\n\nBillions: 900,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,600,000,000\n\nTen millions: 80,000,000 + 60,000,000 = 140,000,000\n\nMillions: 1,000,000 + 9,000,000 = 10,000,000\n\nHundred thousands: 500,000 + 500,000 = 1,000,000\n\nTen thousands: 70,000 + 0 = 70,000\n\nThousands: 4,000 + 7 = 4,007\n\nHundreds: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nTens: 7 + 6 = 13\n\nOnes: 6 + 6 = 12\n\nNow, summing these:\n\n1,600,000,000 + 140,000,000 = 1,740,000,000\n\n1,740,000,000 + 10,000,000 = 1,750,000,000\n\n1,750,000,000 + 1,000,000 = 1,751,000,000\n\n1,751,000,000 + 70,000 = 1,751,070,000\n\n1,751,070,000 + 4,007 = 1,751,074,007\n\n1,751,074,007 + 0 = 1,751,074,007\n\n1,751,074,007 + 13 = 1,751,074,020\n\n1,751,074,020 + 12 = 1,751,074,032\n\nBut according to vertical addition, the sum is 175,180,712. Which is 175 million vs 1.75 billion. The difference is 1,751,074,032 - 175,180,712 = 1,575,893,320. That's a huge difference. There must be a mistake in the component addition.\n\nWait a second, perhaps I messed up the number of digits. Let's check the original numbers again:\n\nFirst number: 981,574,076\n\nThat's 981 million, 574 thousand, 76. So in digits: 9 8 1 5 7 4 0 7 6\n\nSecond number: 769,507,636\n\nThat's 769 million, 507 thousand, 636. In digits: 7 6 9 5 0 7 6 3 6\n\nSo when adding, the digits are:\n\nFirst number: 9 8 1 5 7 4 0 7 6\n\nSecond number: 7 6 9 5 0 7 6 3 6\n\nSo when adding vertically:\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 6 + 6 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 7 + 3 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 0 + 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, no carry\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 7 + 0 = 7 \u2192 7, no carry\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 1 + 9 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8 + 6 + 1 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 9 + 7 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nPosition 10 (billions): 1 \u2192 1\n\nSo the sum is 1 7 5 1 8 0 7 1 2 \u2192 175,180,712.\n\nBut according to component addition, it's 1,751,074,032. Which is 1.75 billion. So there's a factor of 10 difference. This suggests that somewhere in the component addition, I added a component incorrectly. Let's check the ten thousands place.\n\nFirst number's ten thousands place: 70,000\n\nSecond number's ten thousands place: 0\n\nAdding them: 70,000 + 0 = 70,000. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 4,000 + 7 = 4,007. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 0 + 0 = 0. Correct.\n\nTens place: 7 + 6 = 13. Correct.\n\nOnes place: 6 + 6 = 12. Correct.\n\nSo all component additions are correct. Then why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, perhaps the original numbers were misread. Let me check again.\n\nFirst number: 981,574,076\n\nBreaking down:\n\n- 900,000,000\n\n- 80,000,000\n\n- 1,000,000\n\n- 500,000\n\n- 70,000\n\n- 4,000\n\n- 0\n\n- 0\n\n- 7\n\n- 6\n\nSecond number: 769,507,636\n\nBreaking down:\n\n- 700,000,000\n\n- 60,000,000\n\n- 9,000,000\n\n- 500,000\n\n- 0\n\n- 0\n\n- 7\n\n- 6\n\n- 3\n\n- 6\n\nAdding components:\n\nBillions: 900,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,600,000,000\n\nTen millions: 80,000,000 + 60,000,000 = 140,000,000\n\nMillions: 1,000,000 + 9,000,000 = 10,000,000\n\nHundred thousands: 500,000 + 500,000 = 1,000,000\n\nTen thousands: 70,000 + 0 = 70,000\n\nThousands: 4,000 + 7 = 4,007\n\nHundreds: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nTens: 7 + 6 = 13\n\nOnes: 6 + 6 = 12\n\nSumming these:\n\n1,600,000,000 + 140,000,000 = 1,740,000,000\n\n1,740,000,000 + 10,000,0