0=13 \u21923, carry 1\n9. Hundred millions:6 +8=14 +1=15 \u21925, carry 1\n\nNow, after all columns, we have a carryover of 1. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we wrote: 5,3,6,2,2,5,6,8,4.\n\nWait, but that would be 153,622,6384. But according to the calculator, it's 146,917,954. So there's a problem here.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the alignment. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\nFirst number: 66,177,9327. Let's count the digits: 6-6-1-7-7-9-3-2-7. That's 9 digits. So in terms of place values:\n\n- 6: hundred millions\n- 6: ten millions\n- 1: millions\n- 7: hundred thousands\n- 7: ten thousands\n- 9: thousands\n- 3: hundreds\n- 2: tens\n- 7: units\n\nSecond number: 80,736,4957. Digits:8-0-7-3-6-4-9-5-7. Place values:\n\n-8: hundred millions\n-0: ten millions\n-7: millions\n-3: hundred thousands\n-6: ten thousands\n-4: thousands\n-9: hundreds\n-5: tens\n-7: units\n\nSo when adding, the hundred millions place: 6 +8=14, plus carryover 1=15. So write 5, carryover 1.\n\nTen millions place:6 +0=6 +1=7. Write 7, carryover 0.\n\nMillions place:1 +7=8 +0=8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nHundred thousands place:7 +3=10 +0=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:7 +6=13 +1=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place:9 +4=13 +1=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:3 +9=12 +1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:2 +5=7 +1=8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nUnits place:7 +7=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nNow, after all columns, we have a carryover of 1. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we wrote:5,7,8,0,4,4,3,8,4.\n\nSo the number is 157,804,4384? Wait, no. Wait, the digits from left to right are:\n\n1 (carryover), 5 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (units).\n\nSo the number is 157,804,4384. Wait, that's 157 million. But the calculator says 146,917,954. Still discrepancy.\n\nWait, this is really confusing. Let me try adding the numb