ry-over).\n\nSo the total is 1 (ten-billions place) followed by 2 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). So the number is 1,262,148,695. Wait, but that seems high. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add the numbers by breaking them into smaller parts. Let's see:\n\n372,148,610 can be broken into 300,000,000 + 70,000,000 + 2,000,000 + 100,000 + 40,000 + 8,000 + 600 + 10.\n\nSimilarly, 883,994,985 is 800,000,000 + 80,000,000 + 3,000,000 + 900,000 + 90,000 + 4,000 + 900 + 80 + 5.\n\nAdding these parts:\n\n300,000,000 + 800,000,000 = 1,100,000,000\n\n70,000,000 + 90,000,000 = 160,000,000\n\n2,000,000 + 3,000,000 = 5,000,000\n\n100,000 + 900,000 = 1,000,000\n\n40,000 + 10,000 = 50,000\n\n8,000 + 4,000 = 12,000\n\n600 + 900 = 1,500\n\n10 + 80 + 5 = 95\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n1,100,000,000\n\n+160,000,000 = 1,260,000,000\n\n+5,000,000 = 1,265,000,000\n\n+1,000,000 = 1,266,000,000\n\n+50,000 = 1,266,050,000\n\n+12,000 = 1,266,062,000\n\n+1,500 = 1,266,063,500\n\n+95 = 1,266,063,595\n\nWait, that's 1,266,063,595. But earlier, when I did the column addition, I got 1,262,148,695. These two results are different. There must be a mistake somewhere. Let me check the breakdown:\n\nFirst number: 372,148,610\n\nBreaking into parts:\n\n300,000,000 (3*10^8)\n\n70,000,000 (7*10^7)\n\n2,000,000 (2*10^6)\n\n100,000 (1*10^5)\n\n40,000 (4*10^4)\n\n8,000 (8*10^3)\n\n600 (6*10^2)\n\n10 (1*10^1)\n\nSecond number: 883,994,985\n\n800,000,000 (8*10^8)\n\n80,000,000 (8*10^7)\n\n3,000,000 (3*10^6)\n\n900,000 (9*10^5)\n\n90,000 (9*10^4)\n\n4,000 (4*10^3)\n\n900 (9*10^2)\n\n80 (8*10^1)\n\n5 (5*10^0)\n\nAdding the 10^8 places: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n10^7: 7 + 8 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n10^6: 2 + 3 + 1 = 6\n\n10^5: 1 + 9 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n10^4: 4 + 9 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n10^3: 8 + 4 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n10^2: 6 + 9 + 