e number is 15,093,8496, then the digits are 1,5,0,9,3,8,4,9,6. So that's nine digits. So when aligned properly, the digits would be:\n\n          3 2 7 7 7 4 6 7 1\n        + 1 5 0 9 3 8 4 9 6\n        ---------------------------\n\nNow, let's add them column by column from right to left.\n\nStarting with the units place (position 1):\n\n1 (from first number) + 6 (from second number) = 7. Write down 7.\n\nPosition 2: 7 + 9 = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 3: 6 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 4: 7 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 5: 7 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 6: 4 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 7: 7 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 8. Write down 8, carry over 0.\n\nPosition 8: 2 + 5 + 0 (carry) = 7. Write down 7, carry over 0.\n\nPosition 9: 3 + 1 + 0 (carry) = 4. Write down 4.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 (position 1)\n6 (position 2)\n1 (position 3)\n6 (position 4)\n1 (position 5)\n4 (position 6)\n8 (position 7)\n7 (position 8)\n4 (position 9)\n\nSo the sum is 47,871,3467? Wait, hold on. Wait, when we write the digits from right to left, but when we write the number, the first digit we write is the rightmost. Wait, no. Wait, in standard addition, we start from the rightmost digit, but when we write the result, the first digit we get is the units place, then tens, hundreds, etc. So the sum should be written as 47,871,3467? Wait, but that seems like a 9-digit number. Wait, let me check the intermediate steps again.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the carry-over. Let me go through each column step by step.\n\nLet me list the digits of both numbers again:\n\nFirst number (32,777,4671):\nPositions 9 to 1 (left to right):\n3 (10^8 place)\n2 (10^7)\n7 (10^6)\n7 (10^5)\n7 (10^4)\n4 (10^3)\n6 (10^2)\n7 (10^1)\n1 (10^0)\n\nSecond number (15,093,8496):\nPositions 9 to 1 (left to right):\n1 (10^8)\n5 (10^7)\n0 (1