that's 5,862,32702. Which is 586,232,702. But adding this to 140,000,0000 gives 226,862,3302. Which is 226,862,3302. But this is conflicting with previous results.\n\nI think the problem is arising from incorrect alignment of the digits. Let me try adding the two numbers using a different approach.\n\nLet me write both numbers with all digits:\n\nFirst number: 8 1 2 7 0 4 5 1 3\n\nSecond number: 6 4 5 9 1 8 7 8 9\n\nAdding each column from right to left:\n\n1. Units: 3 + 9 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n2. Tens: 1 + 8 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n3. Hundreds: 5 + 7 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4. Thousands: 4 + 1 + 1 = 6 \u2192 6, carry 0\n\n5. Ten thousands: 0 + 9 + 0 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0\n\n6. Hundred thousands: 2 + 5 + 0 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n7. Millions: 1 + 4 + 0 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0\n\n8. Ten millions: 8 + 6 + 0 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n9. Hundred millions: 0 + 0 + 1 = 1 \u2192 1\n\nSo the digits are:\n\n1 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (units)\n\nSo the sum is 145,403,602.\n\nBut when I added the components earlier, I got 145,736,1132. Which is different. So there must be a mistake in the component addition.\n\nWait, let's check the component addition again:\n\nFirst number: 81,270,4513 = 80,000,0000 + 1,200,000 + 270,000 + 4,513\n\nSecond number: 64,591,8789 = 60,000,0000 + 4,500,000 + 91,000 + 8,789\n\nAdding components:\n\n80,000,0000 + 60,000,0000 = 140,000,0000\n\n1,200,000 + 4,500,000 = 5,700,000\n\n270,000 + 91,000 = 361,000\n\n4,513 + 8,789 = 13,302\n\nNow add these:\n\n140,000,0000 + 5,700,000 = 145,700,0000\n\n145,700,0000 + 361,000 = 145,736,1000\n\n145,736,1000 + 13,302 = 145,736,1132\n\nBut according to the vertical addition, the sum is 145,403,602. These two results should be the same, but they are not. Therefore, there must be a mistake in one of the methods.\n\nLet me check the vertical addition again. Maybe I misaligned the digits.\n\nFi