en millions), 5 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 222,313,058\n\nDigits: 2 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nBillions: 4 + 2 = 6\n\nHundred millions: 6 + 2 = 8\n\nTen millions: 5 + 2 = 7\n\nMillions: 3 + 2 = 5\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n\nThousands: 8 + 1 + 1 (carryover) = 10 \u2192 0, carryover 1\n\nHundreds: 4 + 0 + 1 (carryover) = 5\n\nTens: 9 + 5 = 14 \u2192 4, carryover 1\n\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9\n\nWait, so the thousands place is 8 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) = 10. So 0 with carryover 1. Then hundreds place: 4 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) = 5. Then tens place: 9 + 5 = 14. So 4 with carryover 1. Ones place: 1 + 8 = 9.\n\nSo putting all the digits together:\n\nBillions: 6\n\nHundred millions: 8\n\nTen millions: 7\n\nMillions: 5\n\nHundred thousands: 0 (from 7 + 3 + 1)\n\nThousands: 0 (from 8 + 1 + 1)\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 4\n\nOnes: 9\n\nSo the total is 687,600,549. Wait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers digit by digit with proper alignment.\n\nAlternatively, maybe convert the numbers to their numerical values and add.\n\n465,378,491 is 465 million plus 378 thousand plus 491.\n\n222,313,058 is 222 million plus 313 thousand plus 58.\n\nAdding them:\n\n465,378,491 + 222,313,058\n\nLet's add the millions: 465 + 222 = 687 million.\n\nThen the thousands: 378,000 + 313,000 = 691,000.\n\nThen the remaining numbers: 491 + 58 = 549.\n\nSo total is 687,000,000 + 691,000 + 549 = 687,691,549 + 549 = 687,692,098. Wait, that's different from 687,600,549. Hmm, so now I'm confused. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, this discrepancy suggests I made a mistake in my column addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, when adding 465,378,491 