ions), 5 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions). So positions 1 to 9:\n\n1: 1 (hundred millions)\n\n2: 5 (ten millions)\n\n3: 8 (millions)\n\n4: 6 (hundred thousands)\n\n5: 2 (ten thousands)\n\n6: 4 (thousands)\n\n7: 0 (hundreds)\n\n8: 0 (tens)\n\n9: 4 (units)\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Maybe I should just use the standard addition method.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in splitting the numbers. Let me try adding 78,624,0044 and 88,535,8339 step by step.\n\nFirst, let's add the two numbers:\n\n78,624,0044\n\n+88,535,8339\n\nLet me add them digit by digit, starting from the right.\n\nUnits place: 4 + 9 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 4 + 3 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\nHundreds place: 0 + 3 = 3. Write 3.\n\nThousands place: 0 + 8 = 8. Write 8.\n\nTen thousands place: 2 + 5 = 7. Write 7.\n\nHundred thousands place: 6 + 5 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: 8 + 8 = 16 + 1 (carry) = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nTen millions place: 7 + 8 = 15 + 1 (carry) = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nHundred millions place: 0 + 8 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9. Write 9.\n\nSo the result is 967,177,883. Let me check this with another method. Maybe using the fact that 78,624,0044 + 88,535,8339 = ?\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the addition of the two numbers:\n\n78,624,0044\n\n+88,535,8339\n\nLet me add them as:\n\n78,624,0044\n\n+88,535,8339\n\n= (70,000,000 + 80,000,000) + (8,000,000 + 8,000,000) + (600,000 + 500,000) + (20,000 + 30,000) + (4,000 + 5,000) + (0 + 8) + (0 + 3) + (0 + 3) + (4 + 9)\n\nWait, that might not be the right way. Let me break it down:\n\n78,624,0044 = 70,000,000 + 8,000,000 + 600,000 + 20,000 + 4,000 + 0 + 0 + 4 + 4\n\n88,535,8339 = 80,000,000 + 8,000,000 + 500,000 + 30,000 + 5,000 + 800 + 30 + 3 + 9\n\nAdding these together:\n\n70,000,000 + 80,000,000 = 150,000,000\n\n8,000,000 + 8,000,000 = 16,000,000\n\n600,000 + 500,000 = 1,100,000\n\n20,000 + 30,000 = 50,000\n\n4,000 + 5,000 = 9,000\n\n0 + 800 = 800\n\n0 + 30 = 30\n\n0 + 3 = 3\n\n4 + 9 =