ousands)\n\nPosition 8: 4 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 9: 4 (millions)\n\nPosition 10: 4 (ten millions)\n\nSecond number: 80,848,0509\n\nDigits:\n\nPosition 1: 9 (units)\n\nPosition 2: 0 (tens)\n\nPosition 3: 5 (units)\n\nPosition 4: 0 (tens)\n\nPosition 5: 8 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 6: 4 (thousands)\n\nPosition 7: 8 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 8: 0 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 9: 8 (millions)\n\nPosition 10: 0 (ten millions)\n\nSo when adding:\n\nPosition 1: 1 + 9 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 2: 6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7\n\nPosition 3: 0 + 5 = 5\n\nPosition 4: 5 + 0 = 5\n\nPosition 5: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nPosition 6: 9 + 4 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nPosition 7: 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 8: 4 + 0 = 4 + 1 = 5\n\nPosition 9: 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 10: 4 + 0 = 4 + 1 = 5\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nPosition 10: 5\n\nPosition 9: 2\n\nPosition 8: 5\n\nPosition 7: 2\n\nPosition 6: 3\n\nPosition 5: 1\n\nPosition 4: 5\n\nPosition 3: 5\n\nPosition 2: 7\n\nPosition 1: 0\n\nSo the number is 5 2 5 2 3 1 5 5 7 0 \u2192 525,231,5570. But according to the calculator, the correct sum is 125,341,570. This is a contradiction.\n\nWait, maybe the calculator is wrong. Let me check with another method. Let's compute 44,493,5061 + 80,848,0509.\n\nFirst, 44,493,5061 + 80,848,0509.\n\nLet me add the two numbers:\n\n44,493,5061\n\n+80,848,0509\n\n= (44,000,000 + 80,000,000) + (493,5061 + 848,0509)\n\n= 124,000,000 + (493,5061 + 848,0509)\n\nCompute 493,5061 + 848,0509:\n\n493,5061\n\n+848,0509\n\n= (400,000 + 800,000) + (93,5061 + 48,0509)\n\n= 1,200,000 + (93,5061 + 48,0509)\n\nCompute 93,5061 + 48,0509:\n\n93,5061\n\n+48,0509\n\n= (90,000 + 40,000) + (3,5061 + 8,0509)\n\n= 110,000 + (3,5061 + 8,0509)\n\nCompute 3,5061 + 8,0509:\n\n3,5061\n\n+8,0509\n\n= (3,000 + 8,000) + (5061 + 509)\n\n= 11,000 + 5,570\n\n= 16,570\n\nSo total sum:\n\n124,000,000 + 1,200,000 + 16,570 = 125,216,570.\n\nWait, but this is different from the previous result. Now I'm get