\nLet's add the two numbers step by step.\n\nFirst, add 19,092,4711 and 242,825,930.\n\nLet me break it down:\n\n19,092,4711 + 200,000,000 = 39,092,4711\n\nThen add 42,825,930:\n\n39,092,4711 + 42,825,930 = 81,918,4011\n\nWait, but 39,092,4711 + 42,825,930. Let's add the millions: 39 million + 42 million = 81 million. Then the thousands: 092,4711 + 825,930. Wait, this is getting confusing. Maybe I should write them out with commas:\n\n19,092,4711\n+242,825,930\n------------\nLet's add digit by digit, starting from the right.\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711\n\nDigits: 1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1 (assuming the first comma is after the first three digits, so 19,092,4711 is 19 million, 92 thousand, 4711. But 4711 is 4,711. So the number is 19,092,4711. Let's write all digits:\n\n1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930\n\nDigits: 2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0\n\nNow, adding them:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nPosition 1 (units place): 1 + 0 = 1\n\nPosition 2: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nPosition 3: 7 + 9 = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 4: 4 + 5 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 5: 2 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 5.\n\nPosition 6: 9 + 8 = 17. Write down 7, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 7: 0 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 5.\n\nPosition 8: 9 + 2 = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nPosition 9: 1 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 4.\n\nPosition 10: 9 + 4 = 13. Write down 3, carry over 1.\n\nWait, but hold on, the first number has 9 digits, and the second number also has 9 digits. So when adding, we need to align them properly. Let me write them out with the correct number of digits:\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711 (9 digits: 1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1)\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930 (9 digits: 2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0)\n\nLet's align them:\n\n      1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1\n+   2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0\n--------------------------\n\nNow, adding each column:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n1 (units) + 0 = 1\n\nNext (tens place):\n\n1 (tens) + 3 = 4\n\nNext (hundreds place):\n\n7 (hundreds) + 9 = 16. Write 6, carry 1.\n\nNext (thousands place):\n\n4 (thousands) + 5 + 1 (carry) = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\nNext (ten thousands place):\n\n2 (ten thousands) + 2 + 1 (carry) = 5.\n\nNext (hundred thousands place):\n\n9 (hundred thousands) + 8 = 17. Write 7, carry 1.\n\nNext (millions place):\n\n0 (millions) + 4 + 1 (carry) = 5.\n\nNext (ten millions place):\n\n9 (ten millions) + 2 = 11. Write 1, carry 1.\n\nNext (hundred millions place):\n\n1 (hundred millions) + 2 + 1 (carry) = 4.\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the left:\n\n4 (hundred millions)\n\n1 (ten millions)\n\n5 (millions)\n\n7 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n5 (thousands)\n\n4 (hundreds)\n\n6 (tens)\n\n1 (units)\n\nWait, but let me check again. Wait, the leftmost digits:\n\nFirst number's hundred millions place: 1\n\nSecond number's hundred millions place: 2\n\nAdding them: 1 + 2 = 3, plus the carryover 1 (from previous digit) = 4. So the hundred millions place is 4.\n\nTen millions place: First number's 9 (ten millions) + Second number's 4 (ten millions) = 13. Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the alignment.\n\nWait, let's do it step by step:\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1: 1 + 0 = 1\n\n2: 1 + 3 = 4\n\n3: 7 + 9 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n4: 4 + 5 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5: 2 + 2 + 1 = 5\n\n6: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\n7: 0 + 4 + 1 = 5\n\n8: 9 + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n9: 1 + 2 + 1 = 4\n\nSo writing the digits from left to right (highest place to lowest):\n\n4 (hundred millions)\n\n1 (ten millions)\n\n5 (millions)\n\n7 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n5 (thousands)\n\n4 (hundreds)\n\n6 (tens)\n\n1 (units)\n\nSo the sum is 415,705,461.\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n415,705,461.\n\nBut let's check if that's correct. Let's do the addition another way.\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930\n\nAdding them:\n\n19,092,4711\n\n+242,825,930\n\nLet's add 19,092,4711 + 242,825,930.\n\nFirst, add 19,092,4711 + 200,000,000 = 39,092,4711\n\nThen add 42,825,930:\n\n39,092,4711 + 42,825,930\n\n39,092,4711\n\n+42,825,930\n\n=81,918,4011\n\nWait, but 39 million + 42 million is 81 million. Then 92,4711 + 825,930.\n\nWait, 92,4711 is 92 thousand, 4711. 825,930 is 825 thousand, 930.\n\nSo 92,4711 + 825,930 = 92,4711 + 825,930 = 92,4711 + 800,000 = 902,4711; 902,4711 + 25,930 = 928,4011.\n\nThen 81,918,4011 + 928,4011 = 81,918,4011 + 900,000 = 82,818,4011; 82,818,4011 + 28,4011 = 82,846,8022.\n\nWait, this is getting confusing. Maybe I should use another method.\n\nAlternatively, convert both numbers to numbers and add:\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711. Let's parse this as 19,092,4711. So 19 million, 92 thousand, 4711. 4711 is 4,711. So total is 19,092,4711.\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930. That's 242 million, 825,930.\n\nAdding 19,092,4711 and 242,825,930.\n\nLet me convert both to numbers:\n\n19,092,4711 = 19,092,4711\n\n242,825,930 = 242,825,930\n\nAdding them:\n\n19,092,4711\n\n+242,825,930\n\nLet's add the millions: 19 million + 242 million = 261 million.\n\nThen add the remaining parts: 092,4711 + 825,930.\n\n092,4711 is 92,4711. 92,4711 + 825,930.\n\n92,4711 + 800,000 = 892,4711\n\n892,4711 + 25,930 = 892,4711 + 25,930 = 918,4011\n\nSo total is 261,918,4011.\n\nWait, but 261,918,4011 is 261,918,4011. But that seems too high. Wait, 19 million + 242 million is 261 million. Then adding 92 thousand + 825 thousand = 917 thousand. Then 4711 + 930 = 5,641. So total is 261,917,5,641. Wait, that can't be. Wait, maybe I messed up the decimal places.\n\nWait, 19,092,4711 is 19,092,4711. Let's convert that to a number:\n\n19,092,4711 = 19,092,4711\n\n242,825,930 = 242,825,930\n\nAdding them:\n\n19,092,4711\n\n+242,825,930\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with 19,092,4711 + 242,825,930.\n\nFirst, add 19,092,4711 + 200,000,000 = 39,092,4711\n\nThen add 42,825,930:\n\n39,092,4711 + 42,825,930\n\n39,092,4711\n\n+42,825,930\n\n=81,918,4011\n\nWait, 39 million + 42 million is 81 million. Then 92,4711 + 825,930.\n\nWait, 92,4711 is