+ 42,825,930.\n\nWait, 39,092,4711 is 39 million, 92 thousand, 4711. 42,825,930 is 42 million, 825 thousand, 930.\n\nAdding 39 million + 42 million = 81 million.\n\nAdding 92 thousand + 825 thousand = 917 thousand.\n\nAdding 4711 + 930 = 5,641.\n\nSo total is 81,917,5,641. Wait, that's 81,917,5,641. But that can't be right because 81,917,5,641 is 81,917,5,641. But 81,918,4011 + 918,4011 is 82,836,8022. Wait, this is confusing.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the previous digit addition. Let me try again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930\n\nAligning them:\n\n      1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1\n+   2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0\n--------------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n1 (units) + 0 = 1\n\nTens place:\n\n1 (tens) + 3 = 4\n\nHundreds place:\n\n7 (hundreds) + 9 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nThousands place:\n\n4 (thousands) + 5 + 1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTen thousands place:\n\n2 (ten thousands) + 2 + 1 (carry) = 5\n\nHundred thousands place:\n\n9 (hundred thousands) + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nMillions place:\n\n0 (millions) + 4 + 1 (carry) = 5\n\nTen millions place:\n\n9 (ten millions) + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundred millions place:\n\n1 (hundred millions) + 2 + 1 (carry) = 4\n\nSo the sum is 4 1 5 7 0 5 4 6 1 \u2192 415,705,461.\n\nYes, that seems correct. Let me verify by another method. Let's convert both numbers to numbers and add:\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930\n\nAdding them:\n\n19,092,4711 + 242,825,930\n\nLet's add 19,092,4711 + 242,825,930.\n\nFirst, add 19,092,4711 + 200,000,000 = 39,092,4711\n\nThen add 42,825,930:\n\n39,092,4711 + 42,825,930\n\n39,092,4711\n\n+42,825,930\n\n=81,918,4011\n\nWait, but 39,092,4711 + 42,825,930. Let's add the millions: 39 + 42 = 81 million. Then the remaining parts: 092,4711 + 825,930.\n\n092,4711 is 92,4711. 92,4711 + 825,930.\n\n92,4711 + 800,000 = 892,4711\n\n892,4711 + 25,930 = 892,4711 + 25,930 = 918,4011\n\nSo total is 81,918,4011 + 918,4011 = 82,836,8022.\n\nWait, this is conflicting with the previous result. There must be a mistake here. Wait, 39,092,4711 + 42,825,930.\n\nWait, 39,092,4711 is 39 million, 92 thousand, 4711. 42,825,930 is 42 million, 825 thousand, 930.\n\nAdding 39 million + 42 million = 81 million.\n\nAdding 92 thousand + 825 thousand = 917 thousand.\n\nAdding 4711 + 930 = 5,641.\n\nSo total is 81,917,5,641. But 81,917,5,641 is 81,917,5,641. But according to the vertical addition, it's 82,836,8022. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the vertical addition. Let me check again.\n\nVertical addition:\n\n      1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1\n+   2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0\n--------------------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1 + 0 = 1\n\n1 + 3 = 4\n\n7 + 9 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n4 + 5 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n2 + 2 + 1 = 5\n\n9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\n0 + 4 + 1 = 5\n\n9 + 2 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n1 + 2 + 1 = 4\n\nSo the sum is 4 1 5 7 0 5 4 6 1 \u2192 415,705,461.\n\nBut according to the other method, it's 82,836,8022. Which is correct?\n\nWait, let's convert both numbers to numbers and add:\n\nFirst number: 19,092,4711. Let's parse this as 19,092,4711. So 19 million, 92 thousand, 4711. 4711 is 4,711. So total is 19,092,4711.\n\nSecond number: 242,825,930. That's 242,825,930.\n\nAdding them:\n\n19,092,4711 + 242,825,930.\n\nLet me convert 19,092,4711 to 19,092,4711 and 242,825,930 to 242,825,930.\n\nAdding:\n\n19,092,4711\n\n+242,825,930\n\nLet's add the millions:\n\n19 million + 242 million = 261 million.\n\nThen add the remaining parts:\n\n092,4711 + 825,930.\n\n092,4711 is 92,4711. 92,4711 + 825,930.\n\n92,4711 + 800,000 = 892,4711\n\n892,4711 + 25,930 = 892,4711 + 25,930 = 918,4011\n\nSo total is 261,000,000 + 918,4011 = 261,918,4011.\n\nWait, but 261,000,000 + 918,4011 = 261,918,4011. But according to the vertical addition, it's 415,705,461. There's a conflict here. What's wrong?\n\nWait, no. Wait, 19,092,