+ 800,000 = 860,000\n\n7,000 + 500,000 = 507,000\n\n800 + 400 = 1,200\n\n40 + 4 = 44\n\n6 + 4 = 10\n\nNow add all these:\n\n600,000,000 + 31,000,000 = 631,000,000\n\n631,000,000 + 5,000,000 = 636,000,000\n\n636,000,000 + 250,000 = 636,250,000\n\n636,250,000 + 860,000 = 637,110,000\n\n637,110,000 + 507,000 = 637,617,000\n\n637,617,000 + 1,200 = 637,618,200\n\n637,618,200 + 44 = 637,618,244\n\n637,618,244 + 10 = 637,618,254\n\nWait, that's conflicting with the previous result. Wait, this can't be. There must be a mistake here. Let me check the splitting again.\n\nWait, the first number is 111,667,846. Breaking it down:\n\n100,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n10,000,000 (ten million)\n\n1,000,000 (million)\n\n100,000 (ten thousand)\n\n60,000 (thousand)\n\n7,000 (hundred)\n\n800 (ten)\n\n40 (zero?)\n\nWait, no. Wait, 111,667,846 is:\n\n1 (hundred million)\n\n1 (ten million)\n\n1 (million)\n\n6 (hundred thousand)\n\n6 (ten thousand)\n\n7 (thousand)\n\n8 (hundred)\n\n4 (ten)\n\n6 (one)\n\nSo when splitting:\n\n100,000,000 + 10,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 600,000 + 60,000 + 7,000 + 800 + 40 + 6\n\nSimilarly, 524,890,854:\n\n500,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n20,000,000 (ten million)\n\n4,000,000 (million)\n\n800,000 (hundred thousand)\n\n90,000 (ten thousand)\n\n800 (ten)\n\n50 (zero?)\n\n4 (one)\n\nWait, 524,890,854:\n\n500,000,000 + 20,000,000 + 4,000,000 + 800,000 + 90,000 + 800 + 50 + 4\n\nSo adding these:\n\n100,000,000 + 500,000,000 = 600,000,000\n\n10,000,000 + 20,000,000 = 30,000,000\n\n1,000,000 + 4,000,000 = 5,000,000\n\n600,000 + 800,000 = 1,400,000\n\n60,000 + 90,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 800 = 7,800\n\n40 + 50 = 90\n\n6 + 4 = 10\n\nNow adding all these:\n\n600,000,000 + 30,000,000 = 630,000,000\n\n630,000,000 + 5,000,000 = 635,000,000\n\n635,000,000 + 1,400,000 = 636,400,000\n\n636,400,000 + 150,000 = 636,550,000\n\n636,550,000 + 7,800 = 636,557,800\n\n636,557,800 + 90 = 636,557,890\n\n636,557,890 + 10 = 636,557,890 + 10 = 636,557,900\n\nWait, this is conflicting with the previous result. There's a mistake here. Wait, where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, in the first split, the 111,667,846 is:\n\n100,000,000 + 10,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 600,000 + 60,000 + 7,000 + 800 + 40 + 6\n\nBut 600,000 is hundred thousand, 60,000 is ten thousand, 7,000 is thousand, 800 is hundred, 40 is ten, 6 is one.\n\nSimilarly, 524,890,854 is:\n\n500,000,000 + 20,000,000 + 4,000,000 + 800,000 + 90,000 + 800 + 50 + 4\n\nSo adding:\n\n100,000,000 + 500,000,000 = 600,000,000\n\n10,000,000 + 20,000,000 = 30,000,000\n\n1,000,000 + 4,000,000 = 5,000,000\n\n600,000 + 800,000 = 1,400,000\n\n60,000 + 90,000 = 150,000\n\n7,000 + 800 = 7,800\n\n40 + 50 = 90\n\n6 + 4 = 10\n\nNow adding all together:\n\n600,000,000 + 30,000,000 = 630,000,000\n\n630,000,000 + 5,000,000 = 635,000,000\n\n635,000,000 + 1,400,000 = 636,400,000\n\n636,400,000 + 150,000 = 636,550,000\n\n636,550,000 + 7,800 = 636,557,800\n\n636,557,800 + 90 = 636,557,890\n\n636,557,890 + 10 = 636,557,890 + 10 = 636,557,900\n\nBut according to the previous calculation, the sum is 635,706,650. There's a discrepancy here. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the splitting. Let me check the original numbers again.\n\n111,667,846:\n\n- 100,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n- 10,000,000 (ten million)\n\n- 1,000,000 (million)\n\n- 600,000 (hundred thousand)\n\n- 60,000 (ten thousand)\n\n- 7,000 (thousand)\n\n- 800 (hundred)\n\n- 40 (ten)\n\n- 6 (one)\n\nWait, but 600,000 is hundred thousand, 60,000 is ten thousand, 7,000 is thousand, 800 is hundred, 40 is ten, 6 is one. So that's correct.\n\n524,890,854:\n\n- 500,000,000 (hundred million)\n\n- 20,000,000 (ten million)\n\n- 4,000,000 (million)\n\n- 800,000 (hundred thousand)\n\n- 90,000 (ten thousand)\n\n- 800 (hundred)\n\n- 50 (ten)\n\n- 4 (one)\n\nWait, 800,000 is hundred thousand, 90,000 is ten thousand, 800 is hundred, 50 is ten, 4 is one. So that's correct.\n\nSo adding:\n\n600,000,000 + 30,000,000 = 630,000,000\n\n630,000,000 + 5,000,000 = 635,000,000\n\n635,0