41 = 161,758,497\n\nThen 1,500,000,000 + 161,758,497 = 1,661,758,497.\n\nBut according to the column addition, we have 1,661,388,8507. These numbers are different. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute the sum directly using another method. Let's use the fact that 682,961,756 + 978,696,741.\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStart with 682,961,756.\n\nAdd 978,696,741:\n\nFirst, add 900,000,000 to 682,961,756: 682,961,756 + 900,000,000 = 1,582,961,756\n\nThen add 78,696,741 to 1,582,961,756:\n\n1,582,961,756 + 78,696,741:\n\n1,582,961,756\n\n+  78,696,741\n\n= 1,661,658,497\n\nWait, so according to this, the sum is 1,661,658,497. Hmm, now this is different from both previous results. Wait, so now I'm getting 1,661,658,497. What's going on here?\n\nWait, let's do this addition carefully:\n\n1,582,961,756\n\n+  78,696,741\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 + 1 = 7\n\n5 + 4 = 9\n\n7 + 7 = 14 (4, carryover 1)\n\n1 + 6 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\n9 + 9 = 18 (8, carryover 1)\n\n6 + 6 = 12 + 1 = 13 (3, carryover 1)\n\n2 + 7 = 9 + 1 = 10 (0, carryover 1)\n\n8 + 8 = 16 + 1 = 17 (7, carryover 1)\n\n1 + 0 + 1 = 2\n\nWait, but 1,582,961,756:\n\nDigits (from right): 6,5,7,1,9,6,2\n\n78,696,741:\n\nDigits (from right): 1,4,7,6,9,8,7\n\nAdding them:\n\nUnits: 6 + 1 = 7\n\nTens: 5 + 4 = 9\n\nHundreds: 7 + 7 = 14 (4, carryover 1)\n\nThousands: 1 + 6 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nTen-thousands: 9 + 9 = 18 (8, carryover 1)\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 + 6 = 12 + 1 = 13 (3, carryover 1)\n\nMillions: 2 + 8 = 10 + 1 = 11 (1, carryover 1)\n\nTen-millions: 1 + 7 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nHundred-millions: 5 + 9 = 14 + 1 = 15 (5, carryover 1)\n\nWait, but 1,582,961,756 is 1 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (units). Wait, no, wait:\n\nWait, 1,582,961,756:\n\nBreaking down:\n\n1 (hundred millions)\n\n5 (ten millions)\n\n8 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n9 (ten thousands)\n\n6 (thousands)\n\n1 (hundreds)\n\n7 (tens