illions place: first number is 4, second is 8. 4 + 8 = 12. So we write 2 and carry 1. Then, the carry 1 is added to the next higher place, which is the ten millions place. The ten millions place in the first number is 1, and in the second number is 8. So 1 + 8 = 9, plus the carried 1 gives 10. Wait, no. Wait, the carryover from the hundred millions place addition is 1, which is added to the ten millions place. But the ten millions place in the first number is 1 and in the second is 8. So 1 + 8 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. So we write 0 and carry 1. Wait, but that contradicts the previous step.\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me do the addition step by step again, carefully.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n1. Ones place: 0 + 7 = 7. Write 7.\n\n2. Tens place: 4 + 6 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 2 + 9 = 11. 11 + 1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carry 1.\n\n4. Thousands place: 4 + 5 = 9. 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 4 + 5 = 9. 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 3 + 0 = 3. 3 + 1 = 4. Write 4, no carry.\n\n7. Millions place: 7 + 0 = 7. 7 + 1 = 8. Write 8, no carry.\n\n8. Ten millions place: 1 + 8 = 9. 9 + 1 = 10. Write 0, carry 1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place: 4 + 8 = 12. 12 + 1 = 13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n10. Billions place: carryover 1.\n\nSo the digits from highest to lowest are:\n\n1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 7 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,302,400,247.\n\nBut when I added the hundred millions place as 4 + 8 = 12, carry 1, then added that 1 to the next ten millions place (which is 1 + 8 = 9, plus 1 carried over makes 10). Wait, no. Wait, the carryover from the hundred millions place addition is 1, which is added to the ten millions place. The ten millions place in the first number is 1 and the second is 8. So 1 + 8 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. So we write 0 and carry 1. Then the carryover 1 is added to the hundred millions place addition. Wait, no. Wait, the hundred millions place addition was 4 + 8 = 12, which gives 2 and carry 1. Then, the carryover 1 is added to the next higher place, which is the ten millions place. But the ten millions place in the first number is 1 and the second is 8. So 1 + 8 = 9, plus the carried 1 is 10. So we write 0 and carry 1. Then, the carryover 1 is added to the hundred millions place. Wait, no. Wait, the carryover from the hundred millions place addition is 1, which is added to the ten millions place. But the ten millions place is already being added. Wait, this is getting confusing.\n\nWait, perhaps the error is in the order of the digits. Let me try writing the numbers vertically with all digits aligned:\n\n          417,344,240\n        + 880,055,967\n        -------------\n\nBreaking down each number:\n\n417,344,240:\n\nDigits: 4, 1, 7, 3, 4, 4, 2, 4, 0\n\n880,055,967:\n\nDigits: 8, 8, 0, 0, 5, 5, 9, 6, 7\n\nNow, aligning them:\n\n          4 1 7 3 4 4 2 4 0\n        + 8 8 0 0 5 5 9 6 7\n        ---------------------------\n\nNow, adding each column:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position 9):\n\n0 + 7 = 7\n\nPosition 8: 4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 7: 2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 6: 4 + 5 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 1\n\nPosition 5: 4 + 5 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 1\n\nPosition 4: 3 + 0 = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\nPosition 3: 7 + 0 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nPosition 2: 1 + 8 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0\n\nPosition 1: 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nPosition 0: carryover 1 \u2192 1\n\nSo the result is 1 (carryover), followed by the digits from position 1 to 9:\n\nPosition 1: 2\n\nPosition 2: 9\n\nPosition 3: 7\n\nPosition 4: 3\n\nPosition 5: 9\n\nPosition 6: 9\n\nPosition 7: 2\n\nPosition 8: 0\n\nPosition 9: 7\n\nWait, but that would be 1,297,399,207. Wait, no. Wait, the positions are from right to left. Wait, no. Wait, in the vertical addition, the rightmost digit is position 1 (ones),