om 1,297,400,207. Wait, no. Wait, 1,217,344,240 + 55,967:\n\n1,217,344,240\n\n+      55,967\n\n= 1,217,400,207\n\nYes, because 240 + 55,967 = 56,207. So 1,217,344,240 + 55,967 = 1,217,344,240 + 50,000 = 1,217,394,240; then +5,967 = 1,217,394,240 + 5,967 = 1,217,400,207.\n\nBut according to the vertical addition, it's 1,297,390,207. Which is different. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's use the fact that 417,344,240 + 880,055,967 should be equal to 1,297,400,207.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 417,344,240 + 880,055,967:\n\nFirst, add the millions:\n\n417,344,240 has 417 million\n\n880,055,967 has 880 million\n\nAdding those gives 1,297,344,240\n\nWait, 417 + 880 = 1,297 million\n\nThen add the remaining parts: 344,240 + 055,967 = 344,240 + 55,967 = 400,207\n\nSo total is 1,297,000,000 + 400,207 = 1,297,400,207.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the vertical addition must have an error.\n\nGoing back to the vertical addition:\n\n          417,344,240\n\n        + 880,055,967\n\n        -------------\n\nLet me write down the numbers with all digits aligned:\n\n          417,344,240\n\n        + 880,055,967\n\n        = ?\n\nLet's write them out:\n\n417,344,240\n\n+880,055,967\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 + 7 = 7\n\n4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n2 + 9 = 11 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n4 + 5 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 1\n\n4 + 5 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 1\n\n3 + 0 = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\n7 + 0 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n1 + 8 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0\n\n4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n0 + 8 + 1 (carry) = 9\n\nSo the digits are:\n\n1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones)\n\nWait, but according to the step-by-step addition, it's 1,297,400,207. So where is the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait, in the vertical addition, the hundred millions place is 4 + 8 = 12, which gives 2 and carry 1. Then the carry 1 is added to the next higher 