mber: 6 4 6 8 2 4 5 2 8\n\nSecond number: 8 1 4 3 0 4 0 0 8\n\nSo:\n\n      6 4 6 8 2 4 5 2 8\n\n    + 8 1 4 3 0 4 0 0 8\n\n--------------------------\n\nNow, adding each column:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 write 6, carry 1\n\nTens place: 2 + 0 = 2 + 1 (carry) = 3 \u2192 write 3, no carry\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 0 = 2 \u2192 write 2\n\nThousands place: 5 + 4 = 9 \u2192 write 9\n\nTen thousands place: 4 + 4 = 8 \u2192 write 8\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 + 0 = 4 \u2192 write 4\n\nMillions place: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 write 1, carry 1\n\nTen millions place: 6 + 4 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11 \u2192 write 1, carry 1\n\nHundred millions place: 4 + 1 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6 \u2192 write 6\n\nBillions place: 6 + 8 = 14 + 1 (carry) = 15 \u2192 write 5, carry 1\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 is added to the trillions place. So the total is 15,611,198,316?\n\nWait, but let's check the sum step by step:\n\nFirst number: 6,468,245,28\n\nSecond number: 8,143,040,08\n\nAdding them:\n\n6,468,245,28\n\n+8,143,040,08\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with 6,468,245,28 + 8,143,040,08.\n\nFirst, add 8,000,000,000 to 6,468,245,28: 6,468,245,28 + 8,000,000,000 = 14,468,245,28\n\nThen add 143,040,08 to that: 14,468,245,28 + 143,040,08 = ?\n\n14,468,245,28\n\n+  143,040,08\n\n= 14,611,285,36\n\nWait, let's compute that:\n\n14,468,245,28\n\n+  0143,040,08\n\nAligning:\n\n14,468,245,28\n\n+  0143,040,08\n\n= 14,611,285,36\n\nWait, let's do the addition:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n2 + 0 + 1 = 3\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n2 + 4 = 6\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n4 + 0 + 1 = 5\n\n6 + 1 = 7\n\n8 + 0 = 8\n\n1 + 4 = 5\n\n4 (from the first number's hundred millions place) + 0 (from the second number's hundred millions place) + 0 (carryover) = 4\n\nWait, maybe breaking it down:\n\nWait, the first number is 14,468,245,28 and the second is 0143,040,08 (note the leading zero to make it 9 digits):\n\n14,468,245,28\n\n+ 0143,040,08\n\n= 14,611,285,36\n\nYes, because:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n2 + 0 + 1 = 3\n\n5 + 0 = 5\n\n2 + 4 = 6\n\n4 + 0 = 4\n\n8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n4 + 0 + 1 = 5\n\n6 + 1 = 7\n\n8 + 0 = 8\n\n1 + 4 = 5\n\nThen the next digit (hundred millions place): 4 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) + carryover 1 = 5.\n\nSo the total is 14,611,285,36.\n\nWait, but according to the column addition earlier, we had 15,611,198,316. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's compute 6,468,245,28 + 8,143,040,08.\n\nFirst, note that 6,468,245,28 is equal to 6,468,245,28.\n\n8,143,040,08 is equal to 8,143,040,08.\n\nAdding these two:\n\n6,468,245,28\n\n+8,143,040,08\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with 6,468,245,28 + 8,000,000,000 = 14,468,245,28\n\nThen add 143,040,08 to 14,468,245,28:\n\n14,468,245,28 + 143,040,08\n\n= 14,468,245,28 + 100,000,000 = 14,568,245,28\n\n14,568,245,28 + 40,000,000 = 14,608,245,28\n\n14,608,245,28 + 3,000,000 = 14,611,245,28\n\n14,611,245,28 + 40,000 = 14,611,285,28\n\n14,611,285,28 + 8 = 14,611,285,36\n\nSo total is 14,611,285,36.\n\nBut according to the column addition earlier, we had 15,611,198,316. Which is way higher. So there must be a mistake in the column addition.\n\nWait, let's redo the column addition carefully.\n\nFirst number: 6,468,245,28\n\nSecond number: 8,143,040,08\n\nAligning:\n\n      6 4 6 8 2 4 5 2 8\n\n    + 8 1 4 3 0 4 0 0 8\n\n--------------------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\n8 + 8 = 16 \u2192 write 6, carry 1\n\nTens place: 2 + 0 = 2 + 1 (carry) = 3 \u2192 write 3, no carry\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 0 = 2 \u2192 write 2\n\nThousands place: 5 + 4 = 9 \u2192 write 9\n\nTen thousands place: 4 + 4 = 8 \u2192 write 8\n\nHundred thousands place: 4 + 0 = 4 \u2192 write 4\n\nMillions place: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 write 1, carry 1\n\nTen millions place: 6 + 4 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11 \u2192 write 1, carry 1\n\nHundred millions place: 4 + 1 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6 \u2192 write 6\n\nBillions place: 6 + 8 = 14 + 1 (carry) = 15 \u2192 write 5, carry 1\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 is added to the trillions place. So the total is 15,611,198,316? Wait, but according to the step-by-step addition, it's 14,611,285,36. There's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another approach. Let's compute 6,468,245,28 + 8,143,040,08.\n\nFirst, note that 6,468,245,28 is 6,468,245,28.\n\n8,143,040,08 is 8,143,040,08.\n\nAdding these two:\n\n6,468,245,28\n\n+8,143,040,08\n\nLet me add them as:\n\n6,468,245,28\n\n+8,143,040,08\n\n= (6,000,000,000 + 8,000,000,000) + (468,245,28 + 143,040,08)\n\n= 14,000,000,000 + (468,245,28 + 143,040,08)\n\nCompute 468,245,28 + 143,040,08:\n\n468,245,28\n\n+143,040,08\n\n= 611,285,36\n\nTherefore, total is 14,000,000,000 + 611,285,36 = 14,611,285,36.\n\nSo that's 14,611,285,36. Which matches the step-by-step addition. Therefore, the column addition must have been done incorrectly.\n\nSo where did I go wrong in the column addition?\n\nLet me redo the column addition step by step.\n\nFirst number: 6,468,245,28\n\nWhich is:\n\n6 (billions)\n\n4 (hundred millions)\n\n6 (ten millions)\n\n8 (millions)\n\n2 (hundred thousands)\n\n4 (ten thousands)\n\n5 (thousands)\n\n2 (hundreds)\n\n8 (tens)\n\n8 (ones)\n\nSecond number: 8,143,040,08\n\nWhich is:\n\n8 (billions)\n\n1 (hundred millions)\n\n4 (ten millions)\n\n3 (millions)\n\n0 (hundred thousands)\n\n4 (ten thousands)\n\n0 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n8 (ones)\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, the second number is 8,143,040,08. Breaking down:\n\n8 (billion)\n\n1 (hundred million)\n\n4 (ten million)\n\n3 (million)\n\n0 (hundred thousand)\n\n4 (ten thousand)\n\n0 (thousand)\n\n0 (hundred)\n\n8 (ten)\n\n8 (one)\n\nWait, but commas are placed every three digits. So 8,143,040,08 is:\n\n8 (billion), 143 (million), 040 (thousand), 08 (ones). So:\n\n8,000,000