refore, total is 1,745,000,000 + 657,706 = 1,745,657,706.\n\nWait, but according to my previous addition, I got 9,757,862,076. Wait, that's a discrepancy. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, 1,745,657,706 versus 9,757,862,076. Clearly, 1,745,657,706 is a smaller number. So I must have made a mistake in my initial addition.\n\nWait, let's check the second method again. 951,549,283 + 794,108,423.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n951,549,283 = 900,000,000 + 51,549,283  \n794,108,423 = 700,000,000 + 94,108,423  \n\nAdding the millions: 900,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,600,000,000  \nAdding the remaining parts: 51,549,283 + 94,108,423\n\nCompute 51,549,283 + 94,108,423:\n\n51,549,283  \n+94,108,423  \n= ?\n\nAdding units: 3 + 3 = 6  \nTens: 8 + 2 = 10 (0, carry 1)  \nHundreds: 2 + 4 = 6 + 1 = 7  \nThousands: 9 + 8 = 17 (7, carry 1)  \nTen thousands: 4 + 0 = 4 + 1 = 5  \nHundred thousands: 1 + 1 = 2  \nMillions: 5 + 9 = 14 (4, carry 1)  \nTen millions: 1 + 4 = 5 + 1 = 6  \nHundred millions: 0 + 7 = 7  \nBillions: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nWait, but 51,549,283 is 51 million, 549 thousand, 283.  \n94,108,423 is 94 million, 108 thousand, 423.  \nAdding them: 51 + 94 = 145 million, 549 + 108 = 657 thousand, 283 + 423 = 706. So total is 145,657,706. Then adding to 1,600,000,000 gives 1,600,000,000 + 145,657,706 = 1,745,657,706. Which matches the second method. So my initial addition must have been wrong.\n\nTherefore, the correct sum is 1,745,657,706. So where did I go wrong in the first method?\n\nLet me revisit the first method. When I added the hundred millions place: 9 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) = 16. So I wrote down 6 and carried over 1. Then ten millions place: 5 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 15. Wrote down 5, carried over 1. Millions place: 1 (from first number) + 4 (from second number) + 1 (carry) = 6. Hundred thousands place: 5 + 1 = 6. Ten thousands place: 4 + 0 = 4. Thousands place: 9 + 8 = 17. Wrote down 7, carried over 1. Hundreds place: 2 + 4 = 6 + 