ds) + 6 (tens) + 0 (units) = 101,090,560.\n\nBut according to the breakdown, it's 1,009,774,760. So why is there a discrepancy?\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the breakdown. Let me check the breakdown again.\n\n137,931,054 + 871,843,706.\n\nBreakdown:\n\n137,931,054 + 800,000,000 = 937,931,054\n\n937,931,054 + 71,843,706 = 1,009,774,760.\n\nBut 137,931,054 + 871,843,706 = 1,009,774,760 - 800,000,000 + 871,843,706 = 1,009,774,760 - 28,156,294 = 981,618,466. Wait, no. That doesn't make sense.\n\nWait, no. The breakdown is incorrect. Because 137,931,054 + 871,843,706 is not equal to (137,931,054 + 800,000,000) + 71,843,706. It's equal to 137,931,054 + 871,843,706 = 1,009,774,760. So the breakdown is correct. Therefore, the digit-by-digit addition must be wrong.\n\nBut why? Let's check the digit-by-digit addition again.\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the order of the digits. Let me write the numbers vertically with the correct alignment:\n\nFirst number: 137,931,054\n\nSecond number: 871,843,706\n\nSo aligned:\n\n```\n    1 3 7 9 3 1 0 5 4\n  + 8 7 1 8 4 3 7 0 6\n```\n\nBut when adding, the digits should be aligned by their place values. So the units are aligned, tens, hundreds, etc. So the correct alignment is:\n\n```\n     1 3 7 9 3 1 0 5 4\n+    8 7 1 8 4 3 7 0 6\n-----------------------\n```\n\nBut when written without commas, it's:\n\n1 3 7 9 3 1 0 5 4\n\n+8 7 1 8 4 3 7 0 6\n\nBut to add properly, they should be aligned as:\n\n      1 3 7 9 3 1 0 5 4\n+     8 7 1 8 4 3 7 0 6\n-----------------------\nStart from the rightmost digit.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nPosition 1 (units): 4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 0 + 7 = 7\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 3 + 3 = 6\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 1 + 4 = 5\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 3 + 7 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 1 + 8 = 