,000: 1,250,079,816 + 50,000 = 1,250,129,816.\n\nAdding 3,000: 1,250,129,816 + 3,000 = 1,250,132,816.\n\nAdding 200: 1,250,132,816 + 200 = 1,250,133,016.\n\nAdding 27: 1,250,133,016 + 27 = 1,250,133,043.\n\nSo total is 1,250,133,043.\n\nBut according to column addition, it's 616,922,043. So there's a factor of 2 difference. This is impossible. Therefore, one of the methods must be wrong.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the column addition. Let me check the column addition once more.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\nFirst number: 925,779,816\n\nSecond number: 324,353,227\n\nColumn addition:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1. Ones: 6 + 7 = 13. Write 3, carry 1. Correct.\n\n2. Tens: 1 + 2 = 3 + 1 = 4. Correct.\n\n3. Hundreds: 8 + 2 = 10. Write 0, carry 1. Correct.\n\n4. Thousands: 9 + 3 = 12. Write 2, carry 1. Correct.\n\n5. Ten-thousands: 7 + 5 = 12. Write 2, carry 1. Correct.\n\n6. Hundred-thousands: 5 + 3 = 8 + 1 = 9. Correct.\n\n7. Millions: 2 + 4 = 6. Correct.\n\n8. Ten-millions: 9 + 2 = 11. Write 1, carry 1. Correct.\n\n9. Hundred-millions: 2 + 3 = 5 + 1 = 6. Correct.\n\nSo the sum is 616,922,043.\n\nBut according to step-by-step addition, it's 1,250,133,043. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the step-by-step addition. Let me check the addition of 779,816 + 353,227 again.\n\n779,816 + 353,227.\n\nLet me compute this:\n\n779,816 + 353,227.\n\nStart with the ten thousands:\n\n700,000 + 300,000 = 1,000,000.\n\n70,000 + 50,000 = 120,000.\n\n9,000 + 3,000 = 12,000.\n\n800 + 200 = 1,000.\n\n16 + 27 = 43.\n\nTotal: 1,000,000 + 120,000 = 1,120,000; +12,000 = 1,132,000; +1,000 = 1,133,000; +43 = 1,133,043. Correct.\n\nSo 1,249,000,000 + 1,133,043 = 1,250,133,043.\n\nBut according to column addition, it's 616,922,043. So there's a discrepancy of 1,250,133,043 - 616,922,043 = 633,211,000.\n\nThis is a huge difference. Therefore, one of the methods must be wrong. Since the column addition is straightforward and less error-prone, maybe that's the correct one. B