ait, maybe breaking down:\n\n66,5636 = 6*10,000 + 6*1,000 + 5*100 + 6*10 + 3*1 + 6*0\n\n887,0802 = 8*100,000 + 8*10,000 + 7*1,000 + 0*100 + 8*10 + 0*1 + 2*0\n\nAdding them:\n\n10,000: 6 + 0 = 6\n\n1,000: 6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n100: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\n10: 6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n1: 3 + 0 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\n0: 0 + 0 = 0\n\n0: 8 (from 887,0802's hundred thousands place) Wait, no. Wait, 887,0802 is 8*100,000 + 8*10,000 + 7*1,000 + 0*100 + 8*10 + 0*1 + 2*0.\n\nSo when adding 66,5636 and 887,0802:\n\n- 66,5636: 6*10,000 + 6*1,000 + 5*100 + 6*10 + 3*1 + 6*0\n\n- 887,0802: 8*100,000 + 8*10,000 + 7*1,000 + 0*100 + 8*10 + 0*1 + 2*0\n\nSo adding:\n\n10,000: 6 + 0 = 6\n\n1,000: 6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n100: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\n10: 6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n1: 3 + 0 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\n0: 0 + 0 = 0\n\n0: 8 (from 887,0802's hundred thousands place? Wait, no. Wait, 887,0802 is 8*100,000 + 8*10,000 + 7*1,000 + 0*100 + 8*10 + 0*1 + 2*0. So the digits are:\n\nPosition 1 (units): 2\n\n2 (tens): 0\n\n3 (hundreds): 8\n\n4 (thousands): 0\n\n5 (ten thousands): 8\n\n6 (hundred thousands): 7\n\n7 (millions): 8\n\n8 (ten millions): 9\n\n9 (hundred millions): 8\n\nWait, no. Wait, 887,0802 is 8 8 7 0 8 0 2. So positions:\n\nDigit 1: 2 (units)\n\nDigit 2: 0 (tens)\n\nDigit 3: 8 (hundreds)\n\nDigit 4: 0 (thousands)\n\nDigit 5: 8 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit 6: 7 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit 7: 8 (millions)\n\nDigit 8: 9 (ten millions)\n\nDigit 9: 8 (hundred millions)\n\nWait, but 887,0802 is 8 hundred and eighty-seven thousand and eighty-two. So:\n\n- Hundreds place: 8\n\n- Thousands place: 0\n\n- Ten thousands place: 8\n\n- Hundred thousands place: 7\n\n- Millions place: 8\n\n- Ten millions place: 9\n\n- Hundred millions place: 8\n\nWait, that seems conflicting. Wait, 887,0802:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPosition 1: 2 (units)\n\nPosition 2: 0 (tens)\n\nPosition 3: 8 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 4: 0 (thousands)\n\nPosition 5: 8 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 6: 7 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 7: 8 (millions)\n\nPosition 8: 9 (ten millions)\n\nPosition 9: 8 (hundred millions)\n\nSo when adding 66,5636 and 887,0802:\n\n66,5636 is:\n\nPosition 1: 6\n\nPosition 2: 6\n\nPosition 3: 5\n\nPosition 4: 6\n\nPosition 5: 3\n\nPosition 6: 6\n\nPosition 7: 0\n\nPosition 8: 0\n\nPosition 9: 0\n\nWait, no. Wait, 66,5636 is 6 6 5 6 3 6. So positions:\n\nPosition 1: 6 (units)\n\nPosition 2: 6 (tens)\n\nPosition 3: 5 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 4: 6 (thousands)\n\nPosition 5: 3 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 6: 6 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 7: 0 (millions)\n\nPosition 8: 0 (ten millions)\n\nPosition 9: 0 (hundred millions)\n\nWait, but 66,5636 is 66,5636, which is 6*10,000 + 6*1,000 + 5*100 + 6*10 + 3*1 + 6*0.\n\nSo when adding to 887,0802:\n\nPosition 1: 6 + 2 = 8\n\nPosition 2: 6 + 0 = 6\n\nPosition 3: 5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nPosition 4: 6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7\n\nPosition 5: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nPosition 6: 6 + 7 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nPosition 7: 0 + 8 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nPosition 8: 0 + 9 = 9\n\nPosition 9: 0 + 8 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 8 (position 1) 6 (position 2) 3 (position 3) 7 (position 4) 1 (position 5) 3 (position 5) 9 (position 6) 9 (position 7) 8 (position 8) 8 (position 9). Wait, no, this is getting confusing. Let me list the digits step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units):\n\n1. Units: 6 + 2 = 8\n\n2. Tens: 6 + 0 = 6\n\n3. Hundreds: 5 + 8 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4. Thousands: 6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7\n\n5. Ten thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n6. Hundred thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n7. Millions: 0 + 8 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\n8. Ten millions: 0 + 9 = 9\n\n9. Hundred millions: 0 + 8 = 8\n\nSo the digits from left to right are: 8, 6, 3, 7, 1, 3, 9, 9, 8. So the sum is 863,713,986? Wait, but that contradicts the previous result. Wait, no. Wait, if we have digits 8 (units), 6 (tens), 3 (hundreds), 7 (thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 8 (hundred millions). So the number is 863,713,986. Wait, but that's different from the previous 92,537,8438. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me try adding the two numbers directly:\n\n27,066,5636\n\n+89,887,0802\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n      27,066,5636\n    + 89,887,0802\n    -------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n6 + 2 = 8\n\n3 + 0 = 3\n\n6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n5 + 7 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7\n\n0 + 8 = 8\n\n7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\n2 + 9 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n0 + 8 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 92,537,8438. Wait, but when I broke down the numbers into millions and added, I got 963,648. That can't be. Wait, no, 27,066,5636 is 27 million, 89,887,0802 is 89 million. So 27 + 89 = 116 million. Then 66,5636 + 887,0802 = 953,646. So total is 116,953,646. Wait, but according to the digit-by-digit addition, we have 92,537,8438. Which is conflicting.\n\nWait, there's a mistake here. Let me check again. If 27,066,5636 + 89,887,0802:\n\nLet me compute 27,066,5636 + 89,887,0802.\n\nFirst, add 27,066,5636 + 89,887,0802.\n\nLet me use the standard addition method:\n\nStart with the units digit:\n\n6 + 2 = 8\n\nTens digit: 3 + 0 = 3\n\nHundreds digit: 6 + 8 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nThousands digit: 5 + 7 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nTen thousands digit: 6 + 0 = 6 + 1 = 7\n\nHundred thousands digit: 0 + 8 = 8\n\nMillions digit: 7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nTen millions digit: 2 + 9 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nHundred millions digit: 0 + 8 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 92,537,8438. But when I think of 27 million plus 89 million, that's 116 million. Then adding 66,5636 + 887,0802 = 953,646. So total should be 116,953,646. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 92,537,8438. There's a discrepancy here. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, clearly, there's a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 27,066,5636 is 27,066,5636. Let's verify:\n\n27,066,5636:\n\n- 2 (ten