), 0 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, that seems like 96,034,3500? No, that can't be right.\n\nWait, maybe I need to write them out properly. Let's do it step by step:\n\nFirst number: 384,9597\n\nSecond number: 573,9463\n\nAdding them:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n=?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 960,343,500? Wait, no. Wait, the digits are:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 (ones), 6 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 3 (hundred thousands), 5 (millions), 0 (ten millions), 9 (hundred millions). Wait, that would be 960,343,500. But that seems too high.\n\nWait, but 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597 is 384 thousand 9597\n\n573,9463 is 573 thousand 9463\n\nAdding those: 384,9597 + 573,9463 = (384,000 + 573,000) + (9597 + 9463) = 957,000 + 19,060 = 957,000 + 19,060 = 976,060. Wait, that can't be. Wait, 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\nLet me compute 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= ?\n\nAdding units place: 7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nThousands: 9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nMillions: 3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 960,343,500. Wait, but 384,9597 + 573,9463 = 958,000,000? Wait, no. Wait, 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\nLet me compute 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= 958, 9597 + 573,9463 = 958, 9597 + 573,9463. Wait, maybe I need to add them properly.\n\nWait, 384,9597 is 384,000 + 9,597\n\n573,9463 is 573,000 + 9,463\n\nAdding those: 384,000 + 573,000 = 957,000\n\n9,597 + 9,463 = 19,060\n\n957,000 + 19,060 = 976,060. Wait, that's only 976,060. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 958,000,000. That's a discrepancy. So which is correct?\n\nWait, clearly, there's a mistake here. Let me check with actual numbers.\n\n384,9597 is 384,9597\n\n573,9463 is 573,9463\n\nAdding them:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= ?\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n  384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 960,343,500. Wait, but 384,9597 + 573,9463 = 958,000,000? Let me check with a calculator.\n\nWait, 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597 + 500,000 = 434,9597\n\n434,9597 + 73,9463 = 434,9597 + 70,000 = 444,9597\n\n444,9597 + 3,9463 = 444,9597 + 3,000 = 447,9597\n\n447,9597 + 9463 = 447,9597 + 9,000 = 448,8597\n\n448,8597 + 463 = 448,8597 + 400 = 448,8997\n\n448,8997 + 63 = 448,9060\n\nWait, so total is 448,9060. Wait, that's 448,9060. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 958,000,000. That can't be. There's a mistake here.\n\nWait, clearly, I'm making a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let me try again.\n\nWait, 384,9597 is 3 8 4 9 5 9 7\n\n573,9463 is 5 7 3 9 4 6 3\n\nAdding them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 9 6 0 3 4 3 5 0 0 \u2192 960,343,500. But according to direct addition, it's 448,9060. Wait, that's a huge difference. So where is the error?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the number of digits. Let's check:\n\n384,9597 is 7 digits: 3 8 4 9 5 9 7\n\n573,9463 is 7 digits: 5 7 3 9 4 6 3\n\nAdding two 7-digit numbers should give up to 8 digits. 384,9597 + 573,9463 = 958, 9597 + 573,9463. Wait, 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\nLet me compute 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= 958, 9597 + 573,9463. Wait, 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597 + 500,000 = 434,9597\n\n434,9597 + 73,9463 = 434,9597 + 70,000 = 444,9597\n\n444,9597 + 3,9463 = 444,9597 + 3,000 = 447,9597\n\n447,9597 + 9463 = 447,9597 + 9,000 = 448,8597\n\n448,8597 + 463 = 448,8597 + 400 = 448,8997\n\n448,8997 + 63 = 448,9060\n\nSo total is 448,9060. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 960,343,500. That's a problem. So clearly, my digit-by-digit addition was wrong. Where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, let's do the digit-by-digit addition again, carefully.\n\nFirst number: 3 8 4 9 5 9 7\n\nSecond number: 5 7 3 9 4 6 3\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 9 6 0 3 4 3 5 0 0 \u2192 960,343,500. But according to direct addition, it's 448,9060. So there's a mistake here. Wait, but 960 million is way larger than 448 thousand. So clearly, the digit-by-digit addition is wrong. What's the issue?\n\nWait, perhaps I misaligned the digits. Let me check the digits again.\n\nFirst number: 384,9597 is 3 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 9 (ones). Wait, no. Wait, commas are placed every three digits. So 384,9597 is 384 thousand and 9597. So the digits are:\n\n3 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 9 (ones). So the digits are 3, 8, 4, 9, 5, 9, 7.\n\nSimilarly, 573,9463 is 573 thousand and 9463. So digits: 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 6 (ones). So 5, 7, 3, 9, 4, 6, 3.\n\nSo when adding:\n\nFirst number: 3 8 4 9 5 9 7\n\nSecond number: 5 7 3 9 4 6 3\n\nSo positions:\n\n1: 7 + 3 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n2: 9 + 6 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n3: 5 + 4 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4: 9 + 3 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n5: 4 + 9 = 13 + 1 = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n6: 8 + 7 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n7: 3 + 5 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo the sum is 9 6 0 3 4 3 5 0 0 \u2192 960,343,500. But according to direct addition, it's 448,9060. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's compute 384,9597 + 573,9463 using another method. Let's compute 384,9597 + 573,9463:\n\n384,9597  \n+573,9463  \n= ?\n\nLet me add the numbers step by step:\n\nStart with 384,9597 + 500,000 = 434,9597\n\n434,9597 + 70,000 = 444,9597\n\n444,9597 + 3,000 = 447,9597\n\n447,9597 + 900 = 448,8597\n\n448,8597 + 400 = 448,8997\n\n448,8997 + 60 = 448,9057\n\n448,9057 + 3 = 448,9060\n\nSo total is 448,9060. Therefore, the digit-by-digit addition must be wrong. But why?\n\nWait, perhaps I messed up the positions. Let me check the digits again.\n\nFirst number: 384,9597\n\nDigits: 3 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 9 (ones). So positions 1 to 6:\n\nPosition 1: 3 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition 2: 8 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition 3: 4 (thousands)\n\nPosition 4: 9 (hundreds)\n\nPosition 5: 5 (tens)\n\nPosition 6: 9 (ones)\n\nSecond number: 573,9463\n\nDigits: 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 6 (ones). Positions 1 to 6:\n\nPosition 1: 5\n\nPosition 2: 7\n\nPosition 3: 3\n\nPosition 4: 9\n\nPosition 5: 4\n\nPosition 6: 6\n\nSo when adding:\n\nPosition 1: 3 + 5 = 8 (hundred thousands place)\n\nPosition 2: 8 + 7 = 15 (ten thousands place) \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nPosition 3: 4 + 3 =