 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, the numbers are 4,304,577 and 3,837,525.\n\nSo let's align them:\n\n      4,304,577\n\n    +3,837,525\n\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but the first number is 4,304,577. So the digits are:\n\nMillions: 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 3\n\nTen-thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 4\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 7\n\nThe second number is 3,837,525:\n\nMillions: 3\n\nHundred-thousands: 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3\n\nThousands: 7\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 5\n\nWait, so when adding 4,304,577 + 3,837,525, the digits are:\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 3 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2\n\nWait, so that would be:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2\n\nTens: 0\n\nHundreds: 0\n\nThousands: 1\n\nTen-thousands: 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 1 (from 3 + 8 + carry 1)\n\nMillions: 7\n\nSo the sum is 7,141,002. Wait, that's different from before. So 7,141,002. Then total sum would be 400,000,000 + 7,141,002 = 407,141,002. But that's conflicting with the first method. So now I'm confused. Which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the second method. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n104,304,577\n\n303,837,525\n\nFirst method: Adding each digit with carries:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 (tens place) + 2 (tens place) = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 (hundreds place) + 5 (hundreds place) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 (thousands place) + 7 (thousands place) = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 (ten-thousands place) + 3 (ten-thousands place) = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 (hundred-thousands place) + 8 (hundred-thousands place) = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n3 (millions place) + 0 (millions place) = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\n0 (ten-millions place) + 3 (ten-millions place) = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\n1 (hundred-millions place) + 3 (hundred-millions place) = 4 \u2192 4, carry 0\n\nSo the sum is 434,372,032.\n\nSecond method: Breaking into millions:\n\n104,304,577 = 100,000,000 + 4,304,577\n\n303,837,525 = 300,000,000 + 3,837,525\n\nAdding the millions: 100,000,000 + 300,000,000 = 400,000,000\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 4,304,577 + 3,837,525\n\nLet's add these two numbers:\n\n4,304,577\n\n+3,837,525\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but the first number is 4,304,577. So the digits are:\n\nMillions: 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 3\n\nTen-thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 4\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 7\n\nThe second number is 3,837,525:\n\nMillions: 3\n\nHundred-thousands: 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3\n\nThousands: 7\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 5\n\nSo when adding:\n\nMillions place: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nHundred-thousands place: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 3 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands place: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens place: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nOnes place: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2\n\nSo the sum is 7,141,002. Then total sum is 400,000,000 + 7,141,002 = 407,141,002. But this contradicts the first method. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the second method. Let me check the addition of 4,304,577 + 3,837,525 again.\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n      4,304,577\n\n    +3,837,525\n\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 (ones) + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 (tens) + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 (hundreds) + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 (thousands) + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 (ten-thousands) + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 (hundred-thousands) + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 (millions) + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but the first number is 4,304,577. So the digits are:\n\nMillions: 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 3\n\nTen-thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 4\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 7\n\nThe second number is 3,837,525:\n\nMillions: 3\n\nHundred-thousands: 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3\n\nThousands: 7\n\nHundreds: 5\n\nTens: 2\n\nOnes: 5\n\nSo when adding:\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 3 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2\n\nSo the sum is 7,141,002. Then total sum is 400,000,000 + 7,141,002 = 407,141,002. But according to the first method, the sum is 434,372,032. These two results are different. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the alignment when adding the two parts. Let me check the original numbers again:\n\nFirst number: 104,304,577\n\nSecond number: 303,837,525\n\nAdding them:\n\n104,304,577\n\n+303,837,525\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStart with the first number: 104,304,577\n\nAdd 300,000,000 to that: 104,304,577 + 300,000,000 = 404,304,577\n\nNow add the remaining 3,837,525: 404,304,577 + 3,837,525\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n404,304,577\n\n+ 3,837,525\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but 404,304,577:\n\nDigits: 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 7 (ones)\n\nAdding 3,837,525:\n\n3,837,525 is 3 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones)\n\nSo aligning:\n\n      404,304,577\n\n    +  3,837,525\n\n    ------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 (tens) + 2 (tens) = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 (hundreds) + 5 (hundreds) = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 (thousands) + 7 (thousands) = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 (ten thousands) + 3 (ten thousands) = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 (hundred thousands) + 8 (hundred thousands) = 8 + 0 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 (millions) + 3 (millions) = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place: 4 + 0 = 4, since the second number doesn't have a hundred millions place. So the total is 408,142,102. Wait, that's different from both previous results. Now I'm really confused.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step:\n\nFirst number: 104,304,577\n\nSecond number: 303,837,525\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with the ones place: 7 + 5 = 12. Write down 2, carry 1.\n\nTens place: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10. Write down 0, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 5 = 10. Write down 0, carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 4 + 7 = 11. Write down 1, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7. Write down 7, carry 0.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 8 = 8. Write down 8, carry 0.\n\nMillions place: 4 + 3 = 7. Write down 7, carry 0.\n\nTen-millions place: 0 + 3 = 3. Write down 3, carry 0.\n\nHundred-millions place: 1 + 3 = 4. Write down 4.\n\nSo the total is 434,372,032. But when I added 104,304,577 + 300,000,000 = 404,304,577, then added 3,837,525, I got 408,142,102. Which is different. So there's a mistake here.\n\nWait, let's check 404,304,577 + 3,837,525:\n\n404,304,577\n\n+  3,837,525\n\n= ?\n\nLet me add 404,304,577 + 3,000,000 = 407,304,577\n\nThen add 837,525: 407,304,577 + 837,525\n\n407,304,577 + 800,000 = 408,104,577\n\n408,104,577 + 37,525 = 408,142,102\n\nSo that's 408,142,102. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 434,372,032. These two numbers are different. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let me check that again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n104,304,577\n\n303,837,525\n\nDigit-by-digit addition:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nTen-millions: 0 + 3 = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\nHundred-millions: 1 + 3 = 4 \u2192 4\n\nSo the sum is 434,372,032. But when adding step by step, I get 408,142,102. These two numbers are different. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's use the standard addition algorithm.\n\nFirst number: 104,304,577\n\nSecond number: 303,837,525\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n      104,304,577\n\n    + 303,837,525\n\n    -------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 3 = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\n1 + 3 = 4 \u2192 4, carry 0\n\nSo the sum is 434,372,032. Let's verify this by another addition.\n\nLet me compute 104,304,577 + 303,837,525.\n\nAlternatively, note that 303,837,525 = 300,000,000 + 3,837,525.\n\nSo 104,304,577 + 300,000,000 = 404,304,577\n\nThen add 3,837,525 to 404,304,577:\n\n404,304,577 + 3,837,525\n\nLet's compute 404,304,577 + 3,000,000 = 407,304,577\n\nThen add 837,525:\n\n407,304,577 + 800,000 = 408,104,577\n\n408,104,577 + 37,525 = 408,142,102\n\nWait, so this gives 408,142,102. But according to the digit-by-digit addition, it's 434,372,032. These two numbers are different. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n104,304,577\n\n303,837,525\n\nDigit-by-digit:\n\nMillions: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 3 = 3\n\nTen-thousands: 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nThousands: 3 + 3 + 1 = 7\n\nHundreds: 0 + 7 = 7\n\nTens: 4 + 5 = 9\n\nOnes: 5 + 2 = 7\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, this is a different way of breaking it down. Let me try this:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7 + 2 = 9\n\nTens: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 7 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nThousands: 4 + 3 + 1 = 8\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 3 + 1 = 4\n\nMillions: 1 + 0 = 1\n\nWait, this is conflicting. Wait, no, this approach is wrong because the numbers are:\n\nFirst number: 104,304,577\n\nWhich is:\n\n1 (hundred millions)\n\n0 (ten millions)\n\n4 (millions)\n\n3 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n4 (thousands)\n\n5 (hundreds)\n\n7 (tens)\n\n7 (ones)\n\nSecond number: 303,837,525\n\nWhich is:\n\n3 (hundred millions)\n\n0 (ten millions)\n\n3 (millions)\n\n8 (hundred thousands)\n\n3 (ten thousands)\n\n7 (thousands)\n\n5 (hundreds)\n\n2 (tens)\n\n5 (ones)\n\nSo when adding:\n\nHundred millions: 1 + 3 = 4\n\nTen millions: 0 + 0 = 0\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen thousands: 0 + 3 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2\n\nSo the sum is 4 (hundred million), 0 (ten million), 7 (million), 1 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 1 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 0 (ten), 2 (one). So 407,141,002. Wait, that's different from both previous results. Now I'm really confused.\n\nWait, this is getting too confusing. Let me use another approach. Let's use the fact that 104,304,577 + 303,837,525 can be thought of as (100,000,000 + 4,304,577) + (300,000,000 + 3,837,525) = 400,000,000 + (4,304,577 + 3,837,525). Then adding 4,304,577 + 3,837,525.\n\nLet me compute 4,304,577 + 3,837,525:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\n0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\n4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nWait, but 4,304,577 is:\n\n4 (million), 3 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousand), 4 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 7 (ten), 7 (one)\n\n3,837,525 is:\n\n3 (million), 8 (hundred thousand), 3 (ten thousand), 7 (thousand), 5 (hundred), 2 (ten), 5 (one)\n\nAdding them:\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen thousands: 0 + 3 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2\n\nSo the sum is 7,141,002. Then total sum is 400,000,000 + 7,141,002 = 407,141,002. But according to the digit-by-digit addition earlier, it's 434,372,032. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the digit-by-digit addition. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal numbers:\n\n104,304,577\n\n303,837,525\n\nDigit-by-digit addition:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 7 + 5 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nTens: 7 + 2 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 5 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nThousands: 4 + 7 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 3 = 6 + 1 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 + 8 = 8 \u2192 8, carry 0\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7 \u2192 7, carry 0\n\nTen-millions: 0 + 3 = 3 \u2192 3, carry 0\n\nHundred-millions: 1 + 3 = 4 \u2192 4\n\nSo the sum is 434,372,032. But when adding the two parts, I get 407,141,002. These two numbers are different. So which is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with a calculator. Let me veri