t digit. So in the problem, the first digit we got was 0 (units), then 5 (tens), 9 (hundreds), 6 (thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 2 (hundred-thousands), 2 (millions), 7 (ten-millions), 8 (hundred-millions). So writing those digits from left to right (highest place to lowest), the sum is 8 (hundred-millions), 7 (ten-millions), 2 (millions), 5 (hundred-thousands), 2 (ten-thousands), 6 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (units). So the number is 872,256,650.\n\nWait, but let me check this again step by step.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 3 + 7 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nTens: 2 + 2 = 4 + 1 = 5 \u2192 5, carry 0\n\nHundreds: 2 + 7 = 9 \u2192 9, carry 0\n\nThousands: 3 + 3 = 6 \u2192 6, carry 0\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 8 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 8 = 11 + 1 = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\nMillions: 1 + 0 = 1 + 1 = 2 \u2192 2, carry 0\n\nTen-millions: 8 + 9 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nHundred-millions: 6 + 1 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nSo the digits from left to right (hundred-millions to units) are:\n\n8 (hundred-millions), 7 (ten-millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (units). Wait, that would be 872,256,650. But let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another approach to verify. Let's break down the numbers:\n\n681,337,223 = 600,000,000 + 80,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 300,000 + 30,000 + 2,000 + 200 + 20 + 3\n\n109,883,727 = 100,000,000 + 9,000,000 + 8,000,000 + 800,000 + 30,000 + 70,000 + 20,000 + 700 + 20 + 7\n\nAdding them together:\n\n600,000,000 + 100,000,000 = 700,000,000\n\n80,000,000 + 9,000,000 = 89,000,000\n\n1,000,000 + 8,000,000 = 9,000,000\n\n300,000 + 800,000 = 1,100,000\n\n30,000 + 70,000 = 100,000\n\n2,000 + 20,000 = 22,000\n\n200 + 700 = 900\n\n20 + 20 = 40\n\n3 + 7 = 10\n\nNow, adding all these together:\n\n700,000,000 + 89,000,000 = 789,000,000\n\n789,000,000 + 9,000,000 = 798,000,000\n\n798,000,000 + 1,100,000 = 799,100,000\n\n799,100,000 + 100,000 = 