+ 284,165,073 can be broken down into smaller parts.\n\nFor example, 594,836,598 is 500,000,000 + 94,836,598.\n\nSimilarly, 284,165,073 is 200,000,000 + 84,165,073.\n\nAdding the two large parts first: 500,000,000 + 200,000,000 = 700,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 94,836,598 + 84,165,073.\n\nLet me add those two:\n\n94,836,598\n\n+84,165,073\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\n5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\n6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n3 + 6 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n8 + 4 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n4 + 8 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n9 + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, the first number is 94,836,598 and the second is 84,165,073.\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n```\n 94,836,598\n+84,165,073\n------------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 6 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 4 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nMillions place: 4 + 8 = 12 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\nTen-millions place: 9 + 1 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nBillions place: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1\n\nWait, so the sum is 139, 999, 971? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, the first number is 94,836,598:\n\nDigits: 9 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 8 (units)\n\nSecond number is 84,165,073:\n\nDigits: 8 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 3 (units)\n\nAdding them:\n\nTen millions: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nMillions: 4 + 4 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nHundred thousands: 8 + 1 = 9\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 6 = 9\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\nUnits: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1\n\nWait, so the sum is 179,999,971? Wait, no, let me do this step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 6 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nMillions: 4 + 4 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nTen-millions: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nBillions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1\n\nSo the sum is 179,999,971. Wait, that's different from before. Wait, maybe I messed up the breakdown earlier.\n\nWait, the original numbers were 594,836,598 and 284,165,073. When I split 594,836,598 into 500,000,000 + 94,836,598, and 284,165,073 into 200,000,000 + 84,165,073. Then adding 500,000,000 + 200,000,000 = 700,000,000. Then adding 94,836,598 + 84,165,073. But when I did that addition, I got 139,999,971. Wait, but according to the previous step-by-step, it's 179,999,971. Wait, that can't be. There's a mistake here.\n\nWait, no. Wait, 94,836,598 + 84,165,073. Let me check again.\n\nFirst number: 94,836,598\n\nSecond number: 84,165,073\n\nAdding them:\n\nUnits: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 3 + 6 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nMillions: 4 + 4 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nTen-millions: 9 + 8 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nBillions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 1 = 1\n\nSo the sum is 179,999,971. Wait, but 94,836,598 + 84,165,073 = 179,999,971. Then adding that to 700,000,000 gives 700,000,000 + 179,999,971 = 879,999,971. But that contradicts the previous vertical addition where we got 7,188,012,671. Wait, so clearly, there's a mistake here.\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, the original problem is adding 594,836,598 and 284,165,073. If I split 594,836,598 into 500,000,000 + 94,836,598, and 284,165,073 into 200,000,000 + 84,165,073. Then adding 500,000,000 + 200,000,000 = 700,000,000. Then 94,836,598 + 84,165,073 = 179,999,971. Then 700,000,000 + 179,999,971 = 879,999,971. But according to the vertical addition earlier, the sum is 7,188,012,671. These two results should be the same. So there's a discrepancy here. Therefore, one of the methods must be wrong.\n\nWait, let's check the vertical addition again. Let me write down the numbers properly:\n\nFirst number: 594,836,598\n\nSecond number: 284,165,073\n\nAdding them:\n\n```\n 594,836,598\n+284,165,073\n------------\n```\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 8 + 3 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTens: 9 + 7 = 16 + 1 = 17 \u2192 7, carry 1\n\nHundreds: 5 + 0 = 5 + 1 = 6\n\nThousands: 6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nTen-thousands: 8 + 1 = 9 + 1 = 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\nHundred-thousands: 4 + 6 = 10 + 1 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\nMillions: 9 + 8 = 17 + 1 = 18 \u2192 8, carry 1\n\nTen-millions: 5 + 2 = 7 + 1 = 8\n\nHundred-millions: 0 + 0 = 0 + 0 = 0\n\nBillions: 5 + 2 = 7\n\nPutting it all together: 7 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (units). So 7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, the digits are:\n\nBillions: 7\n\nHundred millions: 0\n\nTen millions: 8\n\nMillions: 8\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 1\n\nHundreds: 6\n\nTens: 7\n\nUnits: 1\n\nSo the number is 7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, the places are:\n\nFrom right to left: units, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions, billions.\n\nWait, no. Wait, in standard notation, the places are:\n\nUnits (rightmost), tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions, billions.\n\nSo the sum we have is:\n\nBillions: 7\n\nHundred millions: 0\n\nTen millions: 8\n\nMillions: 8\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 1\n\nHundreds: 6\n\nTens: 7\n\nUnits: 1\n\nSo writing that out: 7 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (units). So the number is 7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, the commas are placed every three digits starting from the right. So:\n\n7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, let's construct the number step by step.\n\nStarting from the highest place:\n\nBillions: 7\n\nHundred millions: 0\n\nTen millions: 8\n\nMillions: 8\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 0\n\nThousands: 1\n\nHundreds: 6\n\nTens: 7\n\nUnits: 1\n\nSo the number is 7 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (units). So written out: 7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, commas are placed every three digits. So:\n\n7 (billions)\n\n088 (millions and hundred thousands)\n\n101 (thousands, ten thousands)\n\n2671? Wait, no. Wait, let's break it down:\n\n- Billions: 7\n- Hundred millions: 0\n- Ten millions: 8\n- Millions: 8\n- Hundred thousands: 1\n- Ten thousands: 0\n- Thousands: 1\n- Hundreds: 6\n- Tens: 7\n- Units: 1\n\nSo the number is 7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, the commas are:\n\n- 7 (billions)\n- 088 (millions and hundred thousands) \u2192 088 is 880,000\n- 101 (thousands, ten thousands) \u2192 101,000\n- 2671? Wait, no. Wait, the remaining digits after 101,000 would be 2671? Wait, no. Wait, let's see:\n\nWait, the number is 7,088,101,2671? No, that can't be. Wait, perhaps I need to write it as:\n\n7,088,101,2671? Wait, no. Wait, the breakdown is:\n\n7 (billions)\n\n0 (hundred millions)\n\n8 (ten millions)\n\n8 (millions)\n\n1 (hundred thousands)\n\n0 (ten thousands)\n\n1 (thousands)\n\n6 (hundreds)\n\n7 (tens)\n\n1 (units)\n\nSo in digits: 7 0 8 8 1 0 1 2 6 7 1. Wait, but that's 11 digits. Wait, 7 (1) billion, 0 (2) hundred millions, 8 (3) ten millions, 8 (4) millions, 1 (5) hundred thousands, 0 (6) 